sends the one the browser accepts. The largest chunk goes from 198 KB to 53 KB with Brotli.\n\nThe cache rule now reads the same as the other servers: files under assets are immutable, everything else is no-cache. Before, anything that was not remoteEntry.js was immutable, which included index.html and the types.\n\nCo-authored-by: Keni Lam <hello@ki-cl.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cc23812d590b2837895ae4aa17c395014174bf42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL-design-system/git/trees/cc23812d590b2837895ae4aa17c395014174bf42"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL-design-system/git/commits/d53e4bda205dd4624d342fdc6671e53a377f74b4","verification":{"payload":"tree cc23812d590b2837895ae4aa17c395014174bf42\nparent efbde83d70cd4ae2726e920e51677d9c18ce04f0\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1791426488 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791426488 -0700\n\nfeat(server): the remote''s files are sent compressed (#42)\n\nThe build writes a .gz and a .br beside each text file with vite-plugin-compression2, and a small middleware sends the one the browser accepts. The largest chunk goes from 198 KB to 53 KB with Brotli.\n\nThe cache rule now reads the same as the other servers: files under assets are immutable, everything else is no-cache. Before, anything that was not remoteEntry.js was immutable, which included index.html and the types.\n\nCo-authored-by: Keni Lam <hello@ki-cl.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxv+4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3X0QAJDuEqej2xu5kS33NTAUrYuU\nE0ON+VF2+03mjqJ5I86CVk3yX6RIk1mV9GLEfeui7HsCDnprzuScYPLl3gbB2Yo2\n2zIPvG3Ox1AmR1NEuno/sUbB7CfYKX+SAx4stbzIJXfjGcXykQkLNlYkF4u/zO9t\ngol5b/60+omGbGHPZ5agBXYihhN68SCNEBrrWngWuHQ8MKA9owbNUIaTArNAbBD3\nrOqGPIvsuTpTCHpfBc/yFlPnWqKG1Mlpbk+ek4zn83b6n/bXrCNdYXe1FWD7yTs8\nBKjIa9gDwCvwQEJ3J6ZGaoa