,{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL-design-system/commits/d56c8cfebbc1c7b59434829657117b5c5eaec332/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T23:41:30Z","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T23:41:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: expose the router as design/router (#10)\n\nRouting lived in Ki.CL''s App/router while HyperLink and the status pages\nhere imported react-router-dom on their own. The router now lives here\nand the host imports it from design/router, so the Router, MatchedRoute,\nuseMatchPattern and the react-router-dom APIs the site uses come from one\nplace. react-router-dom stays a shared singleton, so the host and the\nremote share one router context.\n\nHyperLink and the status pages keep importing react-router-dom directly.\nImporting the router from inside components would create a cycle through\nMatchedRoute, which imports components, and the URLPattern polyfill is\nloaded with a top-level await.\n\nCo-authored-by: Keni Lam <hello@ki-cl.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"aeb89763927e55272df1391ecf1ad179ab1d928f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL-design-system/git/trees/aeb89763927e55272df1391ecf1ad179ab1d928f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL-design-system/git/commits/d56c8cfebbc1c7b59434829657117b5c5eaec332","verification":{"payload":"tree aeb89763927e55272df1391ecf1ad179ab1d928f\nparent 4bb37462eca098b3c4eb8940a8f3067ca557615c\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1791070890 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791070890 -0700\n\nfeat: expose the router as design/router (#10)\n\nRouting lived in Ki.CL''s App/router while HyperLink and the status pages\nhere imported react-router-dom on their own. The router now lives here\nand the host imports it from design/router, so the Router, MatchedRoute,\nuseMatchPattern and the react-router-dom APIs the site uses come from one\nplace. react-router-dom stays a shared singleton, so the host and the\nremote share one router context.\n\nHyperLink and the status pages keep importing react-router-dom directly.\nImporting the router from inside components would create a cycle through\nMatchedRoute, which imports components, and the URLPattern polyfill is\nloaded with a top-level await.\n\nCo-authored-by: Keni Lam <hello@ki-cl.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwZKqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFR0QAK1l+QKfvV2iN3E4Q5WBkdaO\nME9Wx7uKlttjlYX2YUYdzxKCq5EqTJnqOzAdz/X9ogvnNt+YfM4m3JgJoHxhUaD2\nfFbC6PtYnHt7bTrPFrMIiAvw01ZGzk5DcQGHPvVehuG8BPNJuYttU1qDoGqIp6lV\nx+G/9OQ9PGmlD+9gDSVIqLYJDsWwo2mLCqxBMerhM