","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kenilam/Ki.CL-moonshot-exercise/commit/721fcae6b8c410c37d2ce3801301a48d067082e5","node_id":"C_kwDOU6uKFtoAKDcyMWZjYWU2YjhjNDEwYzM3ZDJjZTM4MDEzMDFhNDhkMDY3MDgyZTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kenilam/Ki.CL-moonshot-exercise/commit/a260b3f7b2c808e5f52520d1c87b8690665f8370","sha":"a260b3f7b2c808e5f52520d1c87b8690665f8370","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL-moonshot-exercise/commits/a260b3f7b2c808e5f52520d1c87b8690665f8370"}],"sha":"721fcae6b8c410c37d2ce3801301a48d067082e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL-moonshot-exercise/commits/721fcae6b8c410c37d2ce3801301a48d067082e5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/657845?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kenilam","id":657845,"login":"kenilam","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1Nzg0NQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL-moonshot-exercise/commits/a260b3f7b2c808e5f52520d1c87b8690665f8370/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T09:01:49Z","email":"657845+kenilam@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Keni"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T09:01:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: writing reviewer, federated into Ki.CL (#1)\n\n* feat: scaffold the moonshot module\n\nA Module Federation remote for Ki.CL, mounted at /portfolio/moonshot, that\nalso runs on its own. It consumes the design and api remotes like Ki.CL does\nand gates its routes behind Ki.CL''s sign-in, the same way Pika does.\n\nStandalone, the Vite dev server proxies /design and /api to dev.ki-cl.com\nwith a client token, so a reviewer does not need either repo checked out.\nKi.CL still has to accept that token before this works against dev; locally\nit runs against Ki.CL-back and Ki.CL-design-system.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: writing reviewer, with an introduction page and a Cloud Run image\n\nThe module now does what the exercise asks: paste a commit, PR description,\nREADME or code comment, and Claude Opus 5.5 returns quoted edits per style\nrule that the user accepts or rejects. The server holds the Anthropic key,\nchecks the session with Ki.CL-back and keeps reviews in Mongo.\n\n/portfolio/moonshot is an introduction page (the idea, the design, how to run\nit), and the editor moved to /portfolio/moonshot/writing-review. There is no\nsign-in in the module; standalone, a visitor gets an anonymous session after\nTurnstile, and inside Ki.CL the portfolio''s sign-in covers it.\n\nThe Dockerfile builds the remote and serves it with the API, for the\nki-cl-moonshot services Ki.CL proxies /moonshot to.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: how Ki.CL mounts the remote\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: Cloud Run setup script\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: gcp.sh usage lists every step\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: keep the Cloud Run setup out of the repo\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Keni Lam <admin@loci.world>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"33fdd275fae80e1e0edf2f7c32cbfc14f0dc6ec6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL-moonshot-exercise/git/trees/33fdd275fae80e1e0edf2f7c32cbfc14f0dc6ec6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL-moonshot-exercise/git/commits/a260b3f7b2c808e5f52520d1c87b8690665f8370","verification":{"payload":"tree 33fdd275fae80e1e0edf2f7c32cbfc14f0dc6ec6\nparent 0061141676d570af78b9c6bc7e660a904844a462\nauthor Keni <657845+kenilam@users.noreply.github.com> 1791104509 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791104509 -0700\n\nfeat: writing reviewer, federated into Ki.CL (#1)\n\n* feat: scaffold the moonshot module\n\nA Module Federation remote for Ki.CL, mounted at /portfolio/moonshot, that\nalso runs on its own. It consumes the design and api remotes like Ki.CL does\nand gates its routes behind Ki.CL''s sign-in, the same way Pika does.\n\nStandalone, the Vite dev server proxies /design and /api to dev.ki-cl.com\nwith a client token, so a reviewer does not need either repo checked out.\nKi.CL still has to accept that token before this works against dev; locally\nit runs against Ki.CL-back and Ki.CL-design-system.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: writing reviewer, with an introduction page and a Cloud Run image\n\nThe module now does what the exercise asks: paste a commit, PR description,\nREADME or code comment, and Claude Opus 5.5 returns quoted edits per style\nrule that the user accepts or rejects. The server holds the Anthropic key,\nchecks the session with Ki.CL-back and keeps reviews in Mongo.\n\n/portfolio/moonshot is an introduction page (the idea, the design, how to run\nit), and the editor moved to /portfolio/moonshot/writing-review. There is no\nsign-in in the module; standalone, a visitor gets an anonymous session after\nTurnstile, and inside Ki.CL the portfolio''s sign-in covers it.\n\nThe Dockerfile builds the remote and serves it with the API, for the\nki-cl-moonshot services Ki.CL proxies /moonshot to.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: how Ki.CL mounts the remote\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: Cloud Run setup script\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: gcp.sh usage lists every step\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: keep the Cloud Run setup out of the repo\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Keni Lam <admin@loci.world>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwhX9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjukQACtKUxWN59GJZkXLhsuQnHjp\nY4/2ukT2+/Bx/QjIHi69adUsVI5kmbBGBDWIiie2GNAHWDRN4e06PcXHOn7qmIZK\nWk1DP78jRTDeMVWA+8Pe3KUrMgXkPYZjB8Yeqj6VGtrZeFfUhFIENNLZQLhg4son\nhjNAJr97cyaiFAvE6pGYZAW3oMfF+e1WCesvXyEc06iftH9t7PMyzq9zcC+q+13o\nrP3R0nUQRwLnt3+KVOpWNouTWSrSRBMNjhLn1mauk5k1cCrfmMvK56Jvjy17GWWh\nw2hRIFmWxtA8n8vm2dGFMdWK53sxCyjCgDN8/+TAISBbE33t53sPfY1RUngqvwd6\nTib1XccMjpVbegXBeGsFGFm0DMKHCIClUe7KuIPPyCinOlgsuhzApA2MW4eQIlH7\nOZ0MwiQWxUwiAMfZcoOe4dBH7xT6ppiDj6V+PMZKyl0uOL30CZW8+0xypOp8YcGP\nzjNgLE4yR+RAMiO7CfgVMvmLF1M3r1hDMSwZPIujGx9yZI1ojcxQL/2p8QT8UfFi\nBDwnbix8UqCSo2NgZeyBnlD7eIvfFbYLHL7QiqZ7X42hj5Sv37w28QH5w11UhG4k\n7CWrdWzhR9J7pGGI/h1SDfirVmMGTF24xzNSnQ6Wc2XwUvy1Ove0vvDhA19aVT6x\nSsB+QT8RFWrvBHeJwjTS\n=ZFVK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","veri