ml_url":"https://github.com/vonmiller1/knowledge-centers/commit/f1abc71b14a582a6692bab01a679db74300614cf","node_id":"C_kwDOU7D0zdoAKGYxYWJjNzFiMTRhNTgyYTY2OTJiYWIwMWE2NzlkYjc0MzAwNjE0Y2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vonmiller1/knowledge-centers/commit/945ce7ea58ea30fcabcc64328f91bc0ec15a4f62","sha":"945ce7ea58ea30fcabcc64328f91bc0ec15a4f62","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vonmiller1/knowledge-centers/commits/945ce7ea58ea30fcabcc64328f91bc0ec15a4f62"}],"sha":"f1abc71b14a582a6692bab01a679db74300614cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vonmiller1/knowledge-centers/commits/f1abc71b14a582a6692bab01a679db74300614cf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vonmiller1/knowledge-centers/commits/945ce7ea58ea30fcabcc64328f91bc0ec15a4f62/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:47:14Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:47:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Pin hex-service-kit v0.0.4 (#13)\n\nv0.0.4 closes a silent widening at a tenancy boundary in the federation module.\n_hosted_domain fell back to the email domain before the policy was consulted, so\ntenant_from_hosted_domain meant \"the hd claim OR the mail domain is the tenant\": a\ntoken carrying no hd went from no tenant to a tenant named after its mail domain.\n\nThis repository does not call principal_from_iap_claims, so it was never exposed to\nthat widening; the bump is for one pin across the fleet, and so the fixed function\nis the one available when the claim half is adopted. It also carries the assurance\nand subject-principal knobs that adoption needs.\n\nLockfiles regenerated by fleet-deps.py, never hand-edited. Gate run against the\nnewly installed pin rather than against whatever was already in the venv.","tree":{"sha":"c7ed610297b8b39ae296a01ca494f95f55bb6ea3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vonmiller1/knowledge-centers/git/trees/c7ed610297b8b39ae296a01ca494f95f55bb6ea3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vonmiller1/knowledge-centers/git/commits/945ce7ea58ea30fcabcc64328f91bc0ec15a4f62","verification":{"payload":"tree c7ed610297b8b39ae296a01ca494f95f55bb6ea3\nparent ff3d5850ac37d86a802303e011a07c061f28f940\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787672834 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787672834 +0800\n\nPin hex-service-kit v0.0.4 (#13)\n\nv0.0.4 closes a silent widening at a tenancy boundary in the federation module.\n_hosted_domain fell back to the email domain before the policy was consulted, so\ntenant_from_hosted_domain meant \"the hd claim OR the mail domain is the tenant\": a\ntoken carrying no hd went from no tenant to a tenant named after its mail domain.\n\nThis repository does not call principal_from_iap_claims, so it was never exposed to\nthat widening; the bump is for one pin across the fleet, and so the fixed function\nis the one available when the claim half is adopted. It also carries the assurance\nand subject-principal knobs that adoption needs.\n\nLockfiles regenerated by fleet-deps.py, never hand-edited. Gate run against the\nnewly installed pin rather than against whatever was already in the venv.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjbkCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGKsQADVTLtakukL1ArShs1rmFbYZ\ndGqfOEu56XZq9qp9+P5o9nmQMKMuoUrtbMrggOKQD6cElpTyDrwl37yeFKWoXQz4\nkzAsIu7OX6qSOPtALu3ABYN/nAS4yjqvgqwVyGtQ/8c+3BMz5p4DG5WYihTw9Xfv\nPsj/C1onrTf32g/aWhp1Rynj+sHOJnpl+Wdq7ahz5kj0MNa2dARCnrKaj7zswThP\nXVAFIgGa/JKd0uSlgPMjTgGV5OnYxn+YYdddJga9kMBWTvB0uL5ye9trWLwMZWt6\ncyzXBWuAxULKfvfy3lHRe7DG9yxb26mWRwr33VAhjK+nvCRB646V6mMPuMfnbRdf\nKMuaGgZmE2RFtiT7JGHvwMoQdsN7koVlF7AP1Vx05RnOVpAgvaieVCIwoEEgmr0L\n8oMZ6ZGEO20eb9df4Q7w6rghjO9UZk23oWH9bruDbZ5blo1w9EH243vmUsyjwWPg\n+8LwA686ReUp4u9bCm/Aty6pX9oBicsHcmGorSUX/7sFpMJbdGkqL8KpTceiPI/r\n2Q8kNhCuSXTEEUP4T8WHTu/inTipWkcmAX51amypJr44poB/lT2PFHJngfmOjwFP\nd15FSVI0xGtA2RXfHdg0VlBjrAOnNWVwcIXHled4vTGJQvFsVRf+/6y37DH+TpFH\ntKhvoefmfgDgAgVyZVpQ\n=XG/U\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T08:00:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vonmiller1/knowledge-centers/commit/945ce7ea58ea30fcabcc64328f91bc0ec15a4f62","node_id":"C_kwDOU7D0zdoAKDk0NWNlN2VhNThlYTMwZmNhYmNjNjQzMjhmOTFiYzBlYzE1YTRmNjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vonmiller1/knowledge-centers/commit/ff3d5850ac37d86a802303e011a07c061f28f940","sha":"ff3d5850ac37d86a802303e011a07c061f28f940","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vonmiller1/knowledge-centers/commits/ff3d5850ac37d86a802303e011a07c061f28f940"}],"sha":"945ce7ea58ea30fcabcc64328f91bc0ec15a4f62","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vonmiller1/knowledge-centers/commits/945ce7ea58ea30fcabcc64328f91bc0ec15a4f62"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vonmiller1/knowledge-centers/commits/ff3d5850ac37d86a802303e011a07c061f28f940/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:14:12Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:14:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Bind the IAP transport facts to hex-service-kit v0.0.3 (#12)\n\nWave 2 of the federation migration. Wave 1 moved the eight P0/P1 launch repositories; this is\none of the remaining forty-one.\n\nThe assertion header, the issuer and the key set URL were declared here as literals, and the\nsame three literals are declared again in every repository that verifies an IAP assertion. That\nis one security decision written down once per repo, and a copy that drifts stays green forever,\nbecause a literal always agrees with itself. They are now rebound from hex_service_kit.federation.\n\nObserved failing first. Re-declaring the header while leaving the import in place is caught\nearlier, by ruff F401, so the case only a test can see is the literal re-declared AND the import\ndropped. On that run ruff reported \"All checks passed\" and the only failure was the new test,\nreading ''x-goog-iap-jwt-assert'' against the kit''s ''x-goog-iap-jwt-assertion''. The existing literal\ntest stays, because it catches the other defect, a typo in the published value.\n\nThe pin moves to @v0.0.3 and the locks were rebuilt with org-metadata scripts/fleet-deps.py\nrefresh, which pins the commit the annotated tag dereferences to (d28baa1c). No lockfile was\nhand-edited. v0.0.2 to v0.0.3 moves no dependency.\n\nThis does NOT adopt principal_from_iap_claims. v0.0.3 adds\nFederationPolicy.tenant_from_hosted_domain, which was expected to close the gap that stopped wave\n1 adopting it. Executing this adapter and the kit function against the same claim sets shows they\nstill disagree on four axes, not one, so the tenant and principal half stays local. The four are\nrecorded in the wave-2 report.\n\nGate: make gate, exit 0, 527 passed 1 skipped 2 deselected. Run offline with the v0.0.3 lock installed, so the new\nassertion ran against the release it names.","tree":{"sha":"2e221e85c3666658f8ba02ebce2a774c2a9ba472","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vonmiller1/knowledge-centers/git/trees/2e221e85c3666658f8ba02ebce2a774c2a9ba472"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vonmiller1/knowledge-centers/git/commits/ff3d5850ac37d86a802303e011a07c061f28f940","verification":{"payload":"tree 2e221e85c3666658f8ba02ebce2a774c2a9ba472\nparent 40bc1bb6adbc44281f60196a4af6a07f76bdab57\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787670852 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787670852 +0800\n\nBind the IAP transport facts to hex-service-kit v0.0.3 (#12)\n\nWave 2 of the federation migration. Wave 1 moved the eight P0/P1 launch repositories; this is\none of the remaining forty-one.\n\nThe assertion header, the issuer and the key set URL were declared here as literals, and the\nsame three literals are declared again in every repository that verifies an IAP assertion. That\nis one security decision written down once per repo, and a copy that drifts stays green forever,\nbecause a literal always agrees with itself. They are now rebound from hex_service_kit.federation.\n\nObserved failing first. Re-declaring the header while leaving the import in place is caught\nearlier, by ruff F401, so the case only a test can see is the literal re-declared AND the import\ndropped. On that run ruff reported \"All checks passed\" and the only failure was the new test,\nreading ''x-goog-iap-jwt-assert'' against the kit''s ''x-goog-iap-jwt-assertion''. The existing literal\ntest stays, because it catches the other defect, a typo in the published value.\n\nThe pin moves to @v0.0.3 and the locks were rebuilt with org-metadata scripts/fleet-deps.py\nrefresh, which pins the commit the annotated tag dereferences to (d28baa1c). No lockfile was\nhand-edited. v0.0.2 to v0.0.3 moves no dependency.\n\nThis does NOT adopt principal_from_iap_claims. v0.0.3 adds\nFederationPolicy.tenant_from_hosted_domain, which was expected to close the gap that stopped wave\n1 adopting it. Executing this adapter and the kit function against the same claim sets shows they\nstill disagree on four axes, not one, so the tenant and principal half stays local. The four are\nrecorded in the wave-2 report.\n\nGate: make gate, exit 0, 527 passed 1 skipped 2 deselected. Run offline with the v0.0.3 lock installed, so the new\nassertion ran against the release it names.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjbFECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAltQQAApD6lt1F3jCu1/ibjQaVezW\n9Q8V+hW1a1LFaYqPT1vee0EsUncneGBdJceNEHMSIifldSMg21qL1WZ1jVre6RvD\nXWPb4uv4BAHIy/I11XlUFJYvnlKCyhl4INWOnamMW1PcFEqYC9E8jAKfIj6f7x73\nhV20NLc384vUD2fkWVf4lMAmz/eP+vspEecb5mfI9Gh4ENQCTCMBBtVEe3ySxQRQ\n0ipFwL2eKJtSpAAcRbvAzBdTbseMnHxlikMgx9t1+KJZDDlupbS5wcjRrKTKz4S0\ngqZgFc930QVCljfFNNxmJSUuCKXEPuA/HnUtShQZdBI0Kbo1MqQjykU/6kTl6I2E\n/TzwKb1H9QdGLb8J9V1AnWCpNXfUqshj0qwq10dloWejTzLgbIgzwBKqa7/Et3Bd\nQVi130w1415PRgLvk5N77dnn7aWLjPoZgYyqvOWT8EoPGhsO8rrZng3iq8BXmvEd\nCZ8SnFOj5qyx3TegTNS7NDnjd/ce702U23qv+2AaJgoMYrs1jj61dz1l03+5fUT/\neioH3wo6UU57sb+OrPj7/9i9YXdirrY/h+WWdRbiIxThG4OTNcpFTgx4TaNbumwa\nK3+u+aewIjg1RhPkeQwAXjoYwg86wxuLaKlnsLmsKqBG2wYrE0o+uFKd/CSkjKm2\nWaqW1cITMIcE8NoQRKWc\n=4kXk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T08:00:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/user