","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wtlin1228","id":16910748,"login":"wtlin1228","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2OTEwNzQ4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wtlin1228/frontend-catchup-2026/commits/18081cba2abbc060885cd241b6c7c85dd3584941/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T06:42:11Z","email":"wtlin1228@gmail.com","name":"wtlin1228"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T06:42:11Z","email":"wtlin1228@gmail.com","name":"wtlin1228"},"message":"Fill pattern rows 14-23 in the angular, qwik and sveltekit sheets\n\nEvery framework sheet now maps all 23 patterns. Cells written from memory\nrather than from a port end in \"(verify)\"; docs/README.md says so.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ff512e638718807ef0fd5d4aa4d7fdc6c8a7e6d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wtlin1228/frontend-catchup-2026/git/trees/ff512e638718807ef0fd5d4aa4d7fdc6c8a7e6d0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wtlin1228/frontend-catchup-2026/git/commits/18081cba2abbc060885cd241b6c7c85dd3584941","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16910748?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wtlin1228","id":16910748,"login":"wtlin1228","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2OTEwNzQ4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/wtlin1228/frontend-catchup-2026/commit/18081cba2abbc060885cd241b6c7c85dd3584941","node_id":"C_kwDOU75asNoAKDE4MDgxY2JhMmFiYmMwNjA4ODVjZDI0MWI2YzdjODVkZDM1ODQ5NDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/wtlin1228/frontend-catchup-2026/commit/6cefd7f64287f025f9a920ab3e1c9071a5c3bc2e","sha":"6cefd7f64287f025f9a920ab3e1c9071a5c3bc2e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wtlin1228/frontend-catchup-2026/commits/6cefd7f64287f025f9a920ab3e1c9071a5c3bc2e"}],"sha":"18081cba2abbc060885cd241b6c7c85dd3584941","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wtlin1228/frontend-catchup-2026/commits/18081cba2abbc060885cd241b6c7c85dd3584941"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16910748?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wtlin1228","id":16910748,"login":"wtlin1228","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2OTEwNzQ4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wtlin1228/frontend-catchup-2026/commits/6cefd7f64287f025f9a920ab3e1c9071a5c3bc2e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T04:17:43Z","email":"wtlin1228@gmail.com","name":"wtlin1228"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T04:17:43Z","email":"wtlin1228@gmail.com","name":"wtlin1228"},"message":"Fix page bugs, add dist checker and browser smoke tests, fill sheet rows 14-23\n\nBugs found by driving every page in headless Chrome:\n- dynamic heavy: router started before its view helpers existed (TDZ crash on load)\n- forms heavy: submit validated the hidden attachment-id input, which has no\n  error element, so the form could never be sent\n- security heavy: DOMParser is a Trusted Types sink; a parse-only policy now\n  feeds the sanitiser so rendering through the policy works under enforcement\n- security pages: drop frame-ancestors from the meta CSP (ignored there, logged\n  an error) and explain why it belongs in a header\n- content heavy: active tag was never highlighted (aria-current set to \"\")\n- mock API: posts created via POST had no like counters (NaN on like)\n- partials: `<!-- @variant heavy -->` override so generated article pages mark\n  the heavy variant as current\n- opt the server-rendered form result page into view transitions and skip the\n  transition on the pre-paint guard redirect (Chrome reported aborted transitions)\n\nAdditions:\n- scripts/check-dist.mjs and `pnpm check`: structure, links, assets, anchors,\n  manifest and sitemap checks over dist/, no dependencies\n- tools/smoke: headless-Chrome page and flow tests in their own package\n- dynamic heavy registers search and open-post as WebMCP tools (feature-detected)\n- docs/README.md: caching-model and compile-target measurement rows\n- docs: pattern rows 14-23 in 14 framework sheets (angular, qwik, sveltekit\n  still pending; cells ending in \"(verify)\" were written from memory)\n\nConsistency: twenty-three patterns everywhere, hub list numbers offline as 13,\ngrid wording says up to 200,000 rows, pnpm commands on the static heavy page,\nstatic heavy rubric matches the survey guide.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"197ce5534aad2561c39ed55d6391fe85d68d9e41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wtlin1228/frontend-catchup-2026/git/trees/197ce5534aad2561c39ed55d6391fe85d68d9e41"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wtlin1228/frontend-catchup-2026/git/commits/6cefd7f64287f025f9a920ab3e1c9071a5c3bc2e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16910748?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wtlin1228","id":16910748,"login":"wtlin1228","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2OTEwNzQ4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/wtlin1228/frontend-catchup-2026/commit/6cefd7f64287f025f9a920ab3e1c9071a5c3bc2e","node_id":"C_kwDOU75asNoAKDZjZWZkN2Y2NDI4N2YwMjVmOWE5MjBhYjNlMWM5MDcxYTVjM2JjMmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/wtlin1228/frontend-catchup-2026/commit/bcbd08c62333b947d0f24bb8cb737af0f70a49a0","sha":"bcbd08c62333b947d0f24bb8cb737af0f70a49a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wtlin1228/frontend-catchup-2026/commits/bcbd08c62333b947d0f24bb8cb737af0f70a49a0"}],"sha":"6cefd7f64287f025f9a920ab3e1c9071a5c3bc2e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wtlin1228/frontend-catchup-2026/commits/6cefd7f64287f025f9a920ab3e1c9071a5c3bc2e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16910748?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wtlin1228","id":16910748,"login":"wtlin1228","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2OTEwNzQ4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtlin1228","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wtlin1228/frontend-catchup-2026/commits/bcbd08c62333b947d0f24bb8cb737af0f70a49a0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T01:45:06Z","email":"wtlin1228@gmail.com","name":"wtlin1228"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T01:45:06Z","email":"wtlin1228@gmail.com","name":"wtlin1228"},"message":"Add frontend-baseline: framework-free reference for a framework survey\n\nTwenty-three frontend patterns (static content, forms, routing and data,\nclient state, 3D, real-time, media, cross-cutting concerns, content\npipeline, data grid, composite widgets, motion, offline, async\nconsistency, keep-alive, server functions, sync, morphing, platform\nnavigation, error boundaries, observability, security, styling), each\nas a light page and a heavy page in plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript.\nEach pattern is to be re-implemented per framework and compared against\nthis baseline.\n\nInfrastructure only, no UI framework: Vite 8 for the multi-page build,\nthree.js for the scene pages, marked for Markdown, a self-hosted Roboto.\nFour scripts stand in for what meta-frameworks ship: build-time HTML\npartials with CSP hashes, a mock API (posts, auth, upload, SSE, RPC,\nsync log, CSRF, Server-Timing, app-shell rewrite), a Markdown content\nbuild (pages, index, search, RSS, sitemap) and an image pipeline.\n\nsrc/lib/ holds the few hundred lines every port replaces: DOM helpers,\nan observable store with undo/redo, a router with per-navigation\ncancellation, a fetch cache, RPC batching, local-first sync, DOM\nmorphing, i18n, theme, auth and toasts.\n\ndocs/ has one survey sheet per framework (React, Vue, Svelte, Solid,\nPreact, Qwik, Lit, Alpine, htmx, Angular, Next.js, Nuxt, SvelteKit,\nRemix, React Router, TanStack Start, Astro), a 2026 landscape summary,\nthe survey procedure and rubric, and a sheet template. content-src/\nhas five sample articles for the content pipeline.\n\nUses pnpm (pinned via packageManager) and Node 22.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2f9b7bb9366fbbaf32966efd78cacce085dfd2d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wtlin1228/frontend-catchup-2026/git/trees/2f9b7bb9366fbbaf32966efd78cacce085dfd2d7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wtlin1228/frontend-catchup-2026/git/commits/bcbd08c