nt.com/u/64836476?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman","id":64836476,"login":"sam-bowman","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0ODM2NDc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/17ac28d259bd836d6218208817d8e555d158606b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T17:17:05Z","email":"64836476+sam-bowman@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sam Bowman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T17:17:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: publish multi-arch (amd64/arm64) Docker images (#10)\n\ndocker/setup-qemu-action + a platforms: linux/amd64,linux/arm64 build on\ndocker/build-push-action turns each tagged release''s single-arch image into\na multi-arch manifest, so `docker pull` picks the right one automatically on\neither architecture (e.g. a Raspberry Pi / arm64 NAS).\n\nPrisma''s query/migration engines need their own binary per libc+arch+OpenSSL\ncombination (same class of gap server/Dockerfile already hit once on\namd64/Alpine - see CLAUDE.md), so schema.prisma gains the arm64 musl target\nalongside the existing amd64 one. Missing it wouldn''t fail the build, only\nthe arm64 container at startup - verified for real: built both images for\nlinux/amd64,linux/arm64 via buildx, then actually ran the arm64 server image\n(under QEMU emulation) against a real Postgres database and confirmed clean\nmigrations and a full register round-trip (bcrypt hash, Prisma write, JWT\nissuance) before this was pushed.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"15af138fedeebb67b5870ecd802d5fcee5aeafb6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/trees/15af138fedeebb67b5870ecd802d5fcee5aeafb6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/commits/17ac28d259bd836d6218208817d8e555d158606b","verification":{"payload":"tree 15af138fedeebb67b5870ecd802d5fcee5aeafb6\nparent 78403ded34f3f1946f54a95a562c56b604585afa\nauthor Sam Bowman <64836476+sam-bowman@users.noreply.github.com> 1791393425 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791393425 +0100\n\nfeat: publish multi-arch (amd64/arm64) Docker images (#10)\n\ndocker/setup-qemu-action + a platforms: linux/amd64,linux/arm64 build on\ndocker/build-push-action turns each tagged release''s single-arch image into\na multi-arch manifest, so `docker pull` picks the right one automatically on\neither architecture (e.g. a Raspberry Pi / arm64 NAS).\n\nPrisma''s query/migration engines need their own binary per libc+arch+OpenSSL\ncombination (same class of gap server/Dockerfile already hit once on\namd64/Alpine - see CLAUDE.md), so schema.prisma gains the arm64 musl target\nalongside the existing amd64 one. Missing it wouldn''t fail the build, only\nthe arm64 container at startup - verified for real: built both images for\nlinux/amd64,linux/arm64 via buildx, then actually ran the arm64 server image\n(under QEMU emulation) against a real Postgres database and confirmed clean\nmigrations and a full register round-trip (bcrypt hash, Prisma write, JWT\nissuance) before this was pushed.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP S