ists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commit/e65be1d0926e256ad1b40ea07f874c78994c8f0e","node_id":"C_kwDOU-VlpNoAKGU2NWJlMWQwOTI2ZTI1NmFkMWI0MGVhMDdmODc0Yzc4OTk0YzhmMGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commit/8e2af5b5fbe58ceded914cf59c38e2c5ac9350ae","sha":"8e2af5b5fbe58ceded914cf59c38e2c5ac9350ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/8e2af5b5fbe58ceded914cf59c38e2c5ac9350ae"}],"sha":"e65be1d0926e256ad1b40ea07f874c78994c8f0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/e65be1d0926e256ad1b40ea07f874c78994c8f0e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64836476?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman","id":64836476,"login":"sam-bowman","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0ODM2NDc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/8e2af5b5fbe58ceded914cf59c38e2c5ac9350ae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T16:39:12Z","email":"64836476+sam-bowman@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sam Bowman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T16:39:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add Dockerfiles and publish images to GHCR on release (#8)\n\n* feat: add Dockerfiles and publish images to GHCR on release\n\nAdds server/Dockerfile and client/Dockerfile, and a workflow\n(.github/workflows/publish-images.yml) that builds and pushes both to GHCR\nwhenever release-please cuts a new vX.Y.Z tag - tagged by exact version,\nminor version, and `latest`. Also supports a manual workflow_dispatch rerun\n(e.g. to republish after a base-image security patch) when run against an\nexisting tag.\n\nserver/Dockerfile: multi-stage, non-root, runs `prisma migrate deploy`\nautomatically on container start (server/docker-entrypoint.sh) - same as\nscripts/start.ps1 does for local dev, so nothing to run by hand. Moved\n`prisma` from devDependencies to dependencies in server/package.json since\nthe CLI is now a genuine runtime dependency, not just a dev-time one.\n\nHit and fixed a real Prisma-on-Alpine gap while verifying this actually\nworks (not just that it builds): `binaryTargets` in schema.prisma alone\nwasn''t enough - @prisma/client''s query engine and the `prisma` CLI''s own\nmigration engine do *separate* OpenSSL-version auto-detection, and the\nlatter shells out to an `openssl` binary Alpine doesn''t ship by default.\nMissing either fix fails at a different, unhelpful point: a `prisma\ngenerate` that looks clean, then `prisma migrate deploy` crashing at\ncontainer start with an opaque \"Could not parse schema engine response\"\nerror that never mentions OpenSSL. Needs both `binaryTargets =\n[\"native\", \"linux-musl-openssl-3.0.x\"]` and `apk add openssl` in the image.\n\nclient/Dockerfile: nginx, non-root (redirects the pid file and owns the\ncache dirs, since the base image''s defaults assume root). SPA routing falls\nback to index.html. The real design problem here: Vite bakes VITE_API_URL in\nat *build* time, which would mean a published, reusable image could only\never point at one server unless rebuilt per-deployment. Fixed with a\nruntime-config pattern instead - client/docker-entrypoint.sh regenerates a\nsmall env-config.js from the container''s own API_URL env var on every\nstart, and src/api/client.ts checks window.__RUNTIME_CONFIG__ before falling\nback to the build-time value. One built image, configurable per-deployment.\n\nVerified both images for real, not just that they build: ran the server\ncontainer against real Postgres (migrations applied, full register/login\nround-trip including Prisma/bcrypt/JWT), ran the client container and\nconfirmed env-config.js correctly reflected an injected API_URL, and did a\nfull browser-driven registration through the containerized client hitting\nthe containerized server end to end.\n\nFixed a real config bug along the way: release-please-config.json was\nmissing include-component-in-tag: false, which would have produced tags\nlike `my-chat-app-v0.2.0` instead of the plain `vX.Y.Z` VERSIONING.md and\nthis new workflow both assume - caught before any real tag was ever cut.\n\nREADME, VERSIONING.md, ROADMAP.md, and CLAUDE.md updated accordingly.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: force LF line endings for shell scripts\n\nProtects server/docker-entrypoint.sh and client/docker-entrypoint.sh (added\nin the previous commit) against a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true\nsilently converting their shebang lines to CRLF, which breaks them on Linux\n- exactly where these run (Docker builds, CI). The committed blobs are\nalready LF-only; this just keeps them that way regardless of checkout\nsettings going forward.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0030c340779413f16628e92e5ed5db75a3ac2d8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/trees/0030c340779413f16628e92e5ed5db75a3ac2d8e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/commits/8e2af5b5fbe58ceded914cf59c38e2c5ac9350ae","verification":{"payload":"tree 0030c340779413f16628e92e5ed5db75a3ac2d8e\nparent b4c6b211bce54753c691288011bce1586a2afcb1\nauthor Sam Bowman <64836476+sam-bowman@users.noreply.github.com> 1791391152 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791391152 +0100\n\nfeat: add Dockerfiles and publish images to GHCR on release (#8)\n\n* feat: add Dockerfiles and publish images to GHCR on release\n\nAdds server/Dockerfile and client/Dockerfile, and a workflow\n(.github/workflows/publish-images.yml) that builds and pushes both to GHCR\nwhenever release-please cuts a new vX.Y.Z tag - tagged by exact version,\nminor version, and `latest`. Also supports a manual workflow_dispatch rerun\n(e.g. to republish after a base-image security patch) when run against an\nexisting tag.\n\nserver/Dockerfile: multi-stage, non-root, runs `prisma migrate deploy`\nautomatically on container start (server/docker-entrypoint.sh) - same as\nscripts/start.ps1 does for local dev, so nothing to run by hand. Moved\n`prisma` from devDependencies to dependencies in server/package.json since\nthe CLI is now a genuine runtime dependency, not just a dev-time one.\n\nHit and fixed a real Prisma-on-Alpine gap while verifying this actually\nworks (not just that it builds): `binaryTargets` in schema.prisma alone\nwasn''t enough - @prisma/client''s query engine and the `prisma` CLI''s own\nmigration engine do *separate* OpenSSL-version auto-detection, and the\nlatter shells out to an `openssl` binary Alpine doesn''t ship by default.\nMissing either fix fails at a different, unhelpful point: a `prisma\ngenerate` that looks clean, then `prisma migrate deploy` crashing at\ncontainer start with an opaque \"Could not parse schema engine response\"\nerror that never mentions OpenSSL. Needs both `binaryTargets =\n[\"native\", \"linux-musl-openssl-3.0.x\"]` and `apk add openssl` in the image.\n\nclient/Dockerfile: nginx, non-root (redirects the pid file and owns the\ncache dirs, since the base image''s defaults assume root). SPA routing falls\nback to index.html. The real design problem here: Vite bakes VITE_API_URL in\nat *build* time, which would mean a published, reusable image could only\never point at one server unless rebuilt per-deployment. Fixed with a\nruntime-config pattern instead - client/docker-entrypoint.sh regenerates a\nsmall env-config.js from the container''s own API_URL env var on every\nstart, and src/api/client.ts checks window.__RUNTIME_CONFIG__ before falling\nback to the build-time value. One built image, configurable per-deployment.\n\nVerified both images for real, not just that they build: ran the server\ncontainer against real Postgres (migrations applied, full register/login\nround-trip including Prisma/bcrypt/JWT), ran the client container and\nconfirmed env-config.js correctly reflected an injected API_URL, and did a\nfull browser-driven registration through the containerized client hitting\nthe containerized server end to end.\n\nFixed a real config bug along the way: release-please-config.json was\nmissing include-component-in-tag: false, which would have produced tags\nlike `my-chat-app-v0.2.0` instead of the plain `vX.Y.Z` VERSIONING.md and\nthis new workflow both assume - caught before any real tag was ever cut.\n\nREADME, VERSIONING.md, ROADMAP.md, and CLAUDE.md updated accordingly.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: force LF line endings for shell scripts\n\nProtects server/docker-entrypoint.sh and client/docker-entrypoint.sh (added\nin the previous commit) against a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true\nsilently converting their shebang lines to CRLF, which breaks them on Linux\n- exactly where these run (Docker builds, CI). The committed blobs are\nalready LF-only; this just keeps them that way regardless of checkout\nsettings going forward.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxnWwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFwMQAGnzGhDjfYbNs8S361yIPh2U\njKkfqG+Gm5m2FUmeY6vGguQIGodsHd+MOWS0D1aVzu8p/P+gM/sWhAc3iKHmSZAi\ncF865Tk63tIAbYrKTq0by6//gMe3dowIIzyFdJZp1Gsl6hOC9FQaSG86KPWN1iKg\nli2Gib39YfUefEVogQsPhQ+Sr1XFjKWwoh68fGlnsSLFBt6dTh+O8vWsUKSLvxs5\nsVHrBoXjhAHSYBeQmeuX4g1WmMJgt+xplMRQpTnjWnzU+8ASkJlvN+pWc6bXLVjG\nygh8REjZwZIGWMMFNtyLFa1UMxVntve4V+oNN3n6uy+phFZPRUodU8PQTm4fz+bT\nhvotjM0EFOqor7JdCPwnrehWGYwoh9TdtLZA+tYp22NkgN9Jo5faaUwR/faCECmN\n9i/pWdeHV8j5Oxdekaq8jwKeTJMnzW3uHScDqhs55pyy1V6O6UXZPumXOL42J/Sz\n7Kb12xNWvvyXEnZ4se7TZFqEBd8fJQi1Ru1eCqBU1QuPRoIqE/qQzVYCccsvLWYT\nBjFBCpigt8svQRlvL8T0XYGLD9AJEXc1gGH+uSliHSiGJKKcNMtoi9nyNrK1F+Mo\nuKGAsRsWuDMWjHSrPwEzNrBBnDRaSEQTndA4AG0Fo0N4fiyI0eM4RER9iLFSftZx\neE4Nvjfz+B52JShGSGSU\n=0QCt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T16:39:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commit/8e2af5b5fbe58ceded914cf59c38e2c5ac9350ae","node_id":"C_kwDOU-VlpNoAKDhlMmFmNWI1ZmJlNThjZWRlZDkxNGNmNTljMzhlMmM1YWM5MzUwYWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commit/b4c6b211bce54753c691288011bce1586a2afcb1","sha":"b4c6b211bce54753c691288011bce1586a2afcb1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/b4c6b211bce54753c691288011bce1586a2afcb1"}],"sha":"8e2af5b5fbe58ceded914cf59c38e2c5ac9350ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/8e2af5b5fbe58ceded914cf59c38e2c5ac9350ae"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64836476?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman","id":64836476,"login":"sam-bowman","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0ODM2NDc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/b4c6b211bce54753c691288011bce1586a2afcb1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T16:20:26Z","email":"64836476+sam-bowman@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sam Bowman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T16:20:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: automate versioning and releases with release-please (#6)\n\nReplaces the manual release process documented in VERSIONING.md with\nrelease-please (.github/workflows/release-please.yml): on every push to\nmaster it opens/updates a standing Release PR with the version bump and a\ngenerated CHANGELOG.md entry, built from Conventional Commit PR titles since\nthe last release. Merging that PR - the one deliberate manual step, and what\nactually controls release timing - tags the commit and creates the GitHub\nRelease.\n\nConfigured as a single tracked package at the repo root (release-please-config.json,\n.release-please-manifest.json seeded at the current 0.1.0), with\nserver/package.json and client/package.json kept in sync as \"extra files\"\nrather than independent release components - this isn''t really 3\nseparately-releasable packages, just one app with 3 package.json files for\nworkspace tooling, so treating them as a release-please \"linked group\" would\nhave produced 3 separate CHANGELOG.md files for no benefit. bump-minor-pre-major\nis set so this matches VERSIONING.md''s pre-1.0 rule: breaking changes bump\nMINOR, not MAJOR.\n\nThe workflow uses a PAT (RELEASE_PLEASE_TOKEN secret), not the default\nGITHUB_TOKEN - GitHub Actions deliberately prevents the default token from\ntriggering other workflows when it opens a PR, which would leave the Release\nPR permanently unable to pass master''s required status checks.\n\nUpdates VERSIONING.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, and CLAUDE.md to describe the new\nautomated flow in place of the manual one they documented last PR, and\nCHANGELOG.md to drop the manual [Unreleased] staging section (release-please\nhas no use for it) with a note that entries from here on are generated, not\nhand-edited.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3833f7a2f67108d86f6d8c15dde104dc6f7e3849","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/trees/3833f7a2f67108d86f6d8c15dde104dc6f7e3849"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/commits/b4c6b211bce54753c691288011bce1586a2afcb1","verification":{"payload":"tree 3833f7a2f67108d86f6d8c15dde104dc6f7e3849\nparent beeaf66793cb5bbb706d172e203895a30e5560ee\nauthor Sam Bowman <64836476+sam-bowman@users.noreply.github.com> 1791390026 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791390026 +0100\n\nci: automate versioning and releases with release-please (#6)\n\nReplaces the manual release process documented in VERSIONING.md with\nrelease-please (.github/workflows/release-please.yml): on every push to\nmaster it opens/updates a standing Release PR with the version bump and a\ngenerated CHANGELOG.md entry, built from Conventional Commit PR titles since\nthe last release. Merging that PR - the one deliberate manual step, and what\nactually controls release timing - tags the commit and creates the GitHub\nRelease.\n\nConfigured as a single tracked package at the repo root (release-please-config.json,\n.release-please-manifest.json seeded at the current 0.1.0), with\nserver/package.json and client/package.json kept in sync as \"extra files\"\nrather than independent release components - this isn''t really 3\nseparately-releasable packages, just one app with 3 package.json files for\nworkspace tooling, so treating them as a release-please \"linked group\" would\nhave produced 3 separate CHANGELOG.md files for no benefit. bump-minor-pre-major\nis set so this matches VERSIONING.md''s pre-1.0 rule: breaking changes bump\nMINOR, not MAJOR.\n\nThe workflow uses a PAT (RELEASE_PLEASE_TOKEN secret), not the default\nGITHUB_TOKEN - GitHub Actions deliberately prevents the default token from\ntriggering other workflows when it opens a PR, which would leave the Release\nPR permanently unable to pass master''s required status checks.\n\nUpdates VERSIONING.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, and CLAUDE.md to describe the new\nautomated flow in place of the manual one they documented last PR, and\nCHANGELOG.md to drop the manual [Unreleased] staging section (release-please\nhas no use for it) with a note that entries from here on are generated, not\nhand-edited.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxnFKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAY48QAGUDuZVYF1MRoiqTA1+ZVCVY\nckIKR3GZxjGbLTFl5gxieQqhiZ+5q5Uk8x3FFBzEa7ST310J/3Xxzrm42e8Qngkq\nvZ7Se1ddQ0ml7+lk8L+g5TwDLS82f8ENthWGZwH1v8jrjPTStrOBdc/3OQoq/m5V\nXEt7hLJCo769m1sD4Sa+Ru92fiCdkOf1mtroVeLXXsDB3sKhBlrU/+6R/hjYIsa4\nY8llqXhrnmUmhd1+hF4TD2mdM67i+GKFW6bHVbU0dqDvB5ce3mxatX+9tQZ/2gAM\nyzjwqbBIBireFNffKPr/3TxQ1FJTr+olswcp/9Zj9elT0ZEyDowmpSxc2Jbyd7xu\nfsKV0To3fyBY/5BSbbT0iDAiG/E/BSzq9o1NSKFHETv6BVqLY5sYAi9W46K6/iRo\nIgxdTqGnU4EUoUBg56uLMQkbME8V9VjnLBZF09dhz9dgQdo4nt43rjkOb0nlToSy\nC0HiO2Xxfz71JkRtGr6WrAc5HhHZr5Fl4BSfPYaYjNXp8M2YfpjduaBPgpb0ZHx2\nRZfj0nMJ0c65ADSwXa/MWw9RJq5KBPttVvoJC89fdUSlZQkMg6L6q3a0oHxH3MJH\nM0fn1sWEXTg366O3L8q8cTSfGcUef4pAAfsiwgfuZ0qV6Pj6sCbr/Cg2m/1pgeBu\nJxKsHAL0zI9c+eCgdhIl\n=NhJp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T16:20:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commit/b4c6b211bce54753c691288011bce1586a2afcb1","node_id":"C_kwDOU-VlpNoAKGI0YzZiMjExYmNlNTQ3NTNjNjkxMjg4MDExYmNlMTU4NmEyYWZjYjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commit/beeaf66793cb5bbb706d172e203895a30e5560ee","sha":"beeaf66793cb5bbb706d172e203895a30e5560ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/beeaf66793cb5bbb706d172e203895a30e5560ee"}],"sha":"b4c6b211bce54753c691288011bce1586a2afcb1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/b4c6b211bce54753c691288011bce1586a2afcb1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64836476?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman","id":64836476,"login":"sam-bowman","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0ODM2NDc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/beeaf66793cb5bbb706d172e203895a30e5560ee/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T16:11:45Z","email":"64836476+sam-bowman@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sam Bowman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T16:11:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: add versioning policy, CHANGELOG, and CONTRIBUTING (#5)\n\nVERSIONING.md: semver, applied lockstep across package.json/server/client\n(no client-vs-server compatibility matrix to reason about). Explicitly\npre-1.0 rules apply - breaking changes bump MINOR, not MAJOR, per semver''s\nown carve-out for 0.y.z - and clarifies this is a separate number from\nconfig.protocolVersion, which governs federation wire compatibility and\nchanges independently. Documents the (currently manual) release-cut process\npending the release-automation roadmap item.\n\nCHANGELOG.md: Keep a Changelog format, empty [Unreleased] section ready for\nnew entries, plus a single retrospective [0.1.0] entry built from the actual\ngit history (not reconstructed from memory) summarizing everything shipped\nbefore this file existed.\n\nCONTRIBUTING.md: the actual PR workflow (branch naming, Conventional\nCommits, required CHANGELOG entries), what CI enforces vs. what needs manual\nverification, and code style notes - cross-linked with CLAUDE.md rather than\nduplicating it, since that file is the agent-facing version of the same\nrules.\n\nAlso bumps client/package.json from the untouched Vite scaffold default\n0.0.0 to 0.1.0, matching root and server - the first real application of the\nlockstep policy above. Marks the three corresponding ROADMAP.md items done,\nand links all three new docs from README''s new \"Contributing\" section.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9492ea710f0bedc60baae61d8448fe2728859b25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/trees/9492ea710f0bedc60baae61d8448fe2728859b25"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/commits/beeaf66793cb5bbb706d172e203895a30e5560ee","verification":{"payload":"tree 9492ea710f0bedc60baae61d8448fe2728859b25\nparent 0e0cc872e210e3717e5f55b9ec4dfc66d2907cd4\nauthor Sam Bowman <64836476+sam-bowman@users.noreply.github.com> 1791389505 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791389505 +0100\n\ndocs: add versioning policy, CHANGELOG, and CONTRIBUTING (#5)\n\nVERSIONING.md: semver, applied lockstep across package.json/server/client\n(no client-vs-server compatibility matrix to reason about). Explicitly\npre-1.0 rules apply - breaking changes bump MINOR, not MAJOR, per semver''s\nown carve-out for 0.y.z - and clarifies this is a separate number from\nconfig.protocolVersion, which governs federation wire compatibility and\nchanges independently. Documents the (currently manual) release-cut process\npending the release-automation roadmap item.\n\nCHANGELOG.md: Keep a Changelog format, empty [Unreleased] section ready for\nnew entries, plus a single retrospective [0.1.0] entry built from the actual\ngit history (not reconstructed from memory) summarizing everything shipped\nbefore this file existed.\n\nCONTRIBUTING.md: the actual PR workflow (branch naming, Conventional\nCommits, required CHANGELOG entries), what CI enforces vs. what needs manual\nverification, and code style notes - cross-linked with CLAUDE.md rather than\nduplicating it, since that file is the agent-facing version of the same\nrules.\n\nAlso bumps client/package.json from the untouched Vite scaffold default\n0.0.0 to 0.1.0, matching root and server - the first real application of the\nlockstep policy above. Marks the three corresponding ROADMAP.md items done,\nand links all three new docs from README''s new \"Contributing\" section.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxm9BCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9uQQAGf3lX/9JRp3UBGqgOBBQneo\nkgG+lFpwPBHjPQQLuBc29ITlcsPnHaT4MFvj19fSSjtkVYn/Sh433v8Yb/W4o6s/\nPILDvw0rEwaUFtkIGr5wRYUXbbM30PnMXZn4+BoBqSe4B6Ckb8xDYKBGfYq+O+ON\nXWsA/kCfLQXLT7SgN5JGcjBYwMTSLYSWxq6wFtUWNo+9CiwC79trVC+IZDzQTBxI\n2MiMDmtUW2x5/djUPZOo017DDMI8Cnq5l7jgKRegh88MzwXdPSOTxyAiahm99Qi1\nh8mRzdB2HDB4brucpRCoqDU+m1DD+krw8p0ohUvdrCH1z+cvfcr1aJf0eFAt5YuJ\nbPTQjGqWnrsfDwr03JxQJ6JLtGAc+/YjPEBeGpqyQebjMHd7DNawesgVe53uZD2k\nLOaL/LbXlkSg2/qqryMEd69Ad3VEqGMBNgrp6e3Gv5ATtbettNivwz5c2Nj6oNqz\nzOp2gf1nb9jkQfH5Ni6YllkwSoCk/NMBcEx7aGqJtrxO7MrcXBdU2yOKPMt1Y3O1\nje29wOcXnmPyxWdPXhgMAgcYM03qZDpOaIpaFFe0qj9RufGxfutjhXdQZ45HjA7d\nafn2xHUCrcPsg91YhIbVubJgRyyb4NQRBWpxWo4xjGNimZuxC1d7X+Myme3jXEUK\nUyoBAGvfkQ/1F8Ss3i94\n=+I21\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T16:11:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commit/beeaf66793cb5bbb706d172e203895a30e5560ee","node_id":"C_kwDOU-VlpNoAKGJlZWFmNjY3OTNjYjViYmI3MDZkMTcyZTIwMzg5NWEzMGU1NTYwZWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commit/0e0cc872e210e3717e5f55b9ec4dfc66d2907cd4","sha":"0e0cc872e210e3717e5f55b9ec4dfc66d2907cd4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/0e0cc872e210e3717e5f55b9ec4dfc66d2907cd4"}],"sha":"beeaf66793cb5bbb706d172e203895a30e5560ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/beeaf66793cb5bbb706d172e203895a30e5560ee"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64836476?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman","id":64836476,"login":"sam-bowman","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0ODM2NDc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/0e0cc872e210e3717e5f55b9ec4dfc66d2907cd4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T16:04:43Z","email":"64836476+sam-bowman@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sam Bowman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T16:04:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(server): add Redis-backed cross-replica presence/WS fan-out (#4)\n\nPresence and realtime WebSocket delivery were entirely in-process: a message\nor presence change handled by one server replica had no way to reach a user\nwhose live socket was held open on a different replica behind a load\nbalancer, and a user''s \"online\" status could get confused across replicas\n(one tab connected to replica A, another to replica B). This was the\ndocumented prerequisite blocking the Helm chart item in ROADMAP.md from\nactually working with more than one replica.\n\nOpt-in via REDIS_URL (unset by default - every replica behaves exactly as\nbefore, and a single-replica deployment never touches Redis):\n\n- server/src/lib/redis.ts - lazy pub/sub client factory, returns null with\n  no REDIS_URL set.\n- server/src/ws/presenceFanout.ts - the actual mechanism: sendToUser/\n  sendToUsers now publish to a shared Redis channel instead of writing\n  straight to the local socket map; every replica (including the publisher)\n  subscribes and delivers to whichever target users it has connected\n  locally. Fleet-wide online/offline detection uses short-lived per-\n  connection Redis keys (TTL 90s, refreshed on the existing 30s heartbeat),\n  so a replica that crashes outright just stops refreshing its keys and\n  they expire on their own, rather than leaving someone stuck \"online\"\n  forever.\n- server/src/ws/gateway.ts - rewritten to call through presenceFanout.ts\n  instead of touching its local `connections` map directly for anything\n  cross-replica; the map itself stays local (WebSocket objects can''t be\n  shared across processes) and is still the only thing used for no-Redis\n  single-replica delivery.\n\nVerified two ways:\n- server/test/integration/presenceFanout.test.ts (new, runs against a real\n  Redis service container in CI) - fleet-wide connection counting, TTL\n  expiry, and the core proof that one publish reaches both the publisher''s\n  own subscription and a fully independent subscriber connection standing\n  in for another replica.\n- A live two-process run (two real `tsx` server instances sharing one\n  Redis + one Postgres, real WebSocket clients, not mocked) confirming\n  presence and messages both fan out correctly in both directions, and that\n  disconnecting on one replica correctly flips a user offline as observed\n  from the other.\n\nAlso adds a `redis` service to docker-compose.yml (host port 6380, same\n\"avoid colliding with a native install\" reasoning as Postgres''s 5433) and a\n`redis:7-alpine` service container to the integration-tests CI job, read\nonly by presenceFanout.test.ts - every other integration test still runs\nwith Redis unset, confirmed by running the rest of the suite with the\ncontainer stopped.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4470603ef8ad270a94526d9bf98e80322f8753ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/trees/4470603ef8ad270a94526d9bf98e80322f8753ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/commits/0e0cc872e210e3717e5f55b9ec4dfc66d2907cd4","verification":{"payload":"tree 4470603ef8ad270a94526d9bf98e80322f8753ae\nparent cd2af4d56bc03f232f29ae860c4ff4900d05d063\nauthor Sam Bowman <64836476+sam-bowman@users.noreply.github.com> 1791389083 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791389083 +0100\n\nfeat(server): add Redis-backed cross-replica presence/WS fan-out (#4)\n\nPresence and realtime WebSocket delivery were entirely in-process: a message\nor presence change handled by one server replica had no way to reach a user\nwhose live socket was held open on a different replica behind a load\nbalancer, and a user''s \"online\" status could get confused across replicas\n(one tab connected to replica A, another to replica B). This was the\ndocumented prerequisite blocking the Helm chart item in ROADMAP.md from\nactually working with more than one replica.\n\nOpt-in via REDIS_URL (unset by default - every replica behaves exactly as\nbefore, and a single-replica deployment never touches Redis):\n\n- server/src/lib/redis.ts - lazy pub/sub client factory, returns null with\n  no REDIS_URL set.\n- server/src/ws/presenceFanout.ts - the actual mechanism: sendToUser/\n  sendToUsers now publish to a shared Redis channel instead of writing\n  straight to the local socket map; every replica (including the publisher)\n  subscribes and delivers to whichever target users it has connected\n  locally. Fleet-wide online/offline detection uses short-lived per-\n  connection Redis keys (TTL 90s, refreshed on the existing 30s heartbeat),\n  so a replica that crashes outright just stops refreshing its keys and\n  they expire on their own, rather than leaving someone stuck \"online\"\n  forever.\n- server/src/ws/gateway.ts - rewritten to call through presenceFanout.ts\n  instead of touching its local `connections` map directly for anything\n  cross-replica; the map itself stays local (WebSocket objects can''t be\n  shared across processes) and is still the only thing used for no-Redis\n  single-replica delivery.\n\nVerified two ways:\n- server/test/integration/presenceFanout.test.ts (new, runs against a real\n  Redis service container in CI) - fleet-wide connection counting, TTL\n  expiry, and the core proof that one publish reaches both the publisher''s\n  own subscription and a fully independent subscriber connection standing\n  in for another replica.\n- A live two-process run (two real `tsx` server instances sharing one\n  Redis + one Postgres, real WebSocket clients, not mocked) confirming\n  presence and messages both fan out correctly in both directions, and that\n  disconnecting on one replica correctly flips a user offline as observed\n  from the other.\n\nAlso adds a `redis` service to docker-compose.yml (host port 6380, same\n\"avoid colliding with a native install\" reasoning as Postgres''s 5433) and a\n`redis:7-alpine` service container to the integration-tests CI job, read\nonly by presenceFanout.test.ts - every other integration test still runs\nwith Redis unset, confirmed by running the rest of the suite with the\ncontainer stopped.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxm2bCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKxYQALIXtVbKc1qBdIIBMKPcVjrz\nwsxWhQyG0xGiS5nusAAJSw5Lu455Z5a9V4NYUlcj1Ihc8IeV/jU2J7cbfNqx5JW5\nJQM8YxCjmSOR2+o01j8XmifIbHY/fmfOadRuM8jMRInbzGtGT2tk0jWQ9Cjq1jn/\n6x8DF6iZikdm84KMXgVdbrcXBLUgUGgwPZKx7qgbusGv9vyfqPTb7/JWl5+VamCg\nyAqaPxz8wl4/YRIQkX4OMpPvVomeavXqw51GgfkCjWz/Mmv/NmKxCkNn2/0WjdTq\nJ9/3nY/iFQ9CyyhomAoZZ96ONI/JZuPyjOyS4pOEvgP+mUaRgDjaxaSqIO2T1TS3\n7XLr4xAK0vXX+7rvltEQO6R/KAShz71C7d1C/E3AfI2BQ86sBKPBBgwWLNofMaGB\nIZh9E0GyaYZSo3JzYyqBqvp5NUGNdRDNH4t3kSLCY7bzioM3C9DQkAuZRu0wdNfJ\nRVPz6WYWXCf9//8BJgfE0hu6jKVj6s+iftST7Vlhx9S3tNxPQTAoer46jE2FJEcB\nUCUbSu98oTIVyiagd0egVyTdjMoEdhvlrHRJ1rpx4M7Js7ri5E79JPB5WuOvYxO0\nYdWifndWbx13vYjJkfnnosslhAx4j/Yr/HzK0Skzc3rYUk52vvCYC56ZQ6qdCtKm\np7lcowpdV3NC4binN1Xw\n=Zrr0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T16:04:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commit/0e0cc872e210e3717e5f55b9ec4dfc66d2907cd4","node_id":"C_kwDOU-VlpNoAKDBlMGNjODcyZTIxMGUzNzE3ZTVmNTViOWVjNGRmYzY2ZDI5MDdjZDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commit/cd2af4d56bc03f232f29ae860c4ff4900d05d063","sha":"cd2af4d56bc03f232f29ae860c4ff4900d05d063","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/cd2af4d56bc03f232f29ae860c4ff4900d05d063"}],"sha":"0e0cc872e210e3717e5f55b9ec4dfc66d2907cd4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/0e0cc872e210e3717e5f55b9ec4dfc66d2907cd4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64836476?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman","id":64836476,"login":"sam-bowman","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0ODM2NDc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/cd2af4d56bc03f232f29ae860c4ff4900d05d063/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T17:13:48Z","email":"64836476+sam-bowman@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sam Bowman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T17:13:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: add ROADMAP.md (#3)\n\nCaptures planned work beyond what''s already tracked as a documented gap in\nthe README: desktop/mobile client apps, home-server selection on login,\nfederation protocol completeness, security/production hardening, and\ndeployment infra (Dockerfiles, a full self-host compose file, a Helm\nchart).\n\nFlags one real dependency between two of the infra items: presence and\nrealtime delivery are tracked entirely in-process today\n(server/src/ws/gateway.ts, server/src/modules/presence/presenceStore.ts),\nso a Helm chart that runs more than one replica will silently break\npresence/realtime delivery until that''s fixed - listed as a prerequisite,\nnot a parallel nice-to-have.\n\nLinked from the README''s \"What''s not here yet\" section.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"51b017dc9b67fbe21025aee519d4e5d50f18cde9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/trees/51b017dc9b67fbe21025aee519d4e5d50f18cde9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/commits/cd2af4d56bc03f232f29ae860c4ff4900d05d063","verification":{"payload":"tree 51b017dc9b67fbe21025aee519d4e5d50f18cde9\nparent d48b9aa7017e7003b0503a15a79918ff1a3ca061\nauthor Sam Bowman <64836476+sam-bowman@users.noreply.github.com> 1791306828 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791306828 +0100\n\ndocs: add ROADMAP.md (#3)\n\nCaptures planned work beyond what''s already tracked as a documented gap in\nthe README: desktop/mobile client apps, home-server selection on login,\nfederation protocol completeness, security/production hardening, and\ndeployment infra (Dockerfiles, a full self-host compose file, a Helm\nchart).\n\nFlags one real dependency between two of the infra items: presence and\nrealtime delivery are tracked entirely in-process today\n(server/src/ws/gateway.ts, server/src/modules/presence/presenceStore.ts),\nso a Helm chart that runs more than one replica will silently break\npresence/realtime delivery until that''s fixed - listed as a prerequisite,\nnot a parallel nice-to-have.\n\nLinked from the README''s \"What''s not here yet\" section.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxSxMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6l0QACoH1Ekrb+bjC/OHUnxqqzbQ\nKxSsYPJOYSZBSVTSEaShHLcSrjvwktGIW4Tk54FpN4xi/so1rF6RpwgqHR26i3ii\nALL1jhH7QVKlw9ThM/Ljai0iGw/1Kdw/AOcfF1Jr6DszaryKjePyUzC64YmYs5XJ\nF416iSH16ziAb9f/X03Jb+2JTKx7MkU1IBCS4zpeO4mP5bTzBGbMAnDOTj3OjKbw\nagBAgT091isuaxNyg9jBZl9BqB3mt61CjfznBeIfZMjQonGgFWIYFXvEsfPYJTg7\nThlFAA5bClUj+7LMbiBAAOZFZH96/SA0YATSDDIlpDuSVX1bu2+EHuW308CKNiL8\nk+l/tMDR2/OTT9LQnikUo0djA6HwbyWhVM9Kno6lyEcPadcrjY5mwPMQ7vnpYSbi\naxlFVd2hxdiS3PPvYHI0E4O3bmIBiUNVPY4Grj24rqMahlFPA/vzVi7MOF9G+cDC\nJ5zLItqHn8oCRlSJFipad16jx9iBdg0KjSnzgGlDQ2rVJ1S0Dyi57+4/DAXItzcs\nOK7B/g+2whLpVuSlA83b3ko7b1j9GVNfzk0XMlkzPrCcEnQDHSgQjubABz0TzdWy\nxViuHzSc0/kf4Y4Y5A+OAqvgG/aYXRucvZuiTgNU74kDdbc7opfwYDdqk9pf2sE+\n7w0snNRFZC9uNOhuAGQu\n=B0O1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T17:13:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commit/cd2af4d56bc03f232f29ae860c4ff4900d05d063","node_id":"C_kwDOU-VlpNoAKGNkMmFmNGQ1NmJjMDNmMjMyZjI5YWU4NjBjNGZmNDkwMGQwNWQwNjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commit/d48b9aa7017e7003b0503a15a79918ff1a3ca061","sha":"d48b9aa7017e7003b0503a15a79918ff1a3ca061","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/d48b9aa7017e7003b0503a15a79918ff1a3ca061"}],"sha":"cd2af4d56bc03f232f29ae860c4ff4900d05d063","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/cd2af4d56bc03f232f29ae860c4ff4900d05d063"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64836476?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman","id":64836476,"login":"sam-bowman","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0ODM2NDc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/d48b9aa7017e7003b0503a15a79918ff1a3ca061/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T17:07:07Z","email":"64836476+sam-bowman@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sam Bowman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T17:07:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: add MIT license and README status badges (#2)\n\nThe README has called this an \"open-source\" project since the start, but\nthere was no actual LICENSE file backing that up. Adds MIT (the standard\ndefault for a project already positioning itself this way) and a license\nfield to each workspace''s package.json.\n\nAlso adds a badge row to the README: live CI status (pulls from the actual\nci.yml workflow run, not a static claim), license, last commit, and open\nissue count - all dynamic/verifiable, nothing that can silently go stale\nthe way the earlier gitleaks doc claim did. Plus a small static tech-stack\nrow (Node, TypeScript, React, PostgreSQL) for at-a-glance context.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0f173f6183acc47715db976ccc6a1ee87acc86f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/trees/0f173f6183acc47715db976ccc6a1ee87acc86f4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/commits/d48b9aa7017e7003b0503a15a79918ff1a3ca061","verification":{"payload":"tree 0f173f6183acc47715db976ccc6a1ee87acc86f4\nparent 021863f88f475a3aee24c694be7ec5bda8b3a867\nauthor Sam Bowman <64836476+sam-bowman@users.noreply.github.com> 1791306427 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791306427 +0100\n\ndocs: add MIT license and README status badges (#2)\n\nThe README has called this an \"open-source\" project since the start, but\nthere was no actual LICENSE file backing that up. Adds MIT (the standard\ndefault for a project already positioning itself this way) and a license\nfield to each workspace''s package.json.\n\nAlso adds a badge row to the README: live CI status (pulls from the actual\nci.yml workflow run, not a static claim), license, last commit, and open\nissue count - all dynamic/verifiable, nothing that can silently go stale\nthe way the earlier gitleaks doc claim did. Plus a small static tech-stack\nrow (Node, TypeScript, React, PostgreSQL) for at-a-glance context.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxSq7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1xAQAKSzDm6PQ0veqU7Ffjo1MX91\nSKAyA6uoyDsvImfLKRa5E6o9c/qnaUH3zi3w/UEuyIiX/xK+Vf3hEkm4PZMboXuJ\nh0PtdtvazWr24ZHynI58oJBe6I2Sohu/RVkqoskTbu28ufpgBbBHqJpJMObjJJl3\nG+e1Ft62QHqVSeT6vsow65TbrA2R9EYGIOR6/TMxjeNDG1zTimUgAAhM568oiXtw\nHN3tRkt7kDZuHU5UTU84PdONSBxBmhDPTQ4se7tGmZrdcMae3ijV9p4Lw/c9kXZl\nf+9jCn9MfwusTtf8j7xq2rApknn/o13sZ2HboXitw/KwJ5/5uxpgCRZ6Kkxmn8fQ\nFtXXqH4GYcakKRojhh5OIR926dDM7upxMcfxtbESAbJQuylS8NtTQI11PRlNleF7\nEig6qIDf0LSQZpU7D2pEw0u7dD8Fv0hOJtnMlqhuzcBR7Y9XN5fM+eUWz/hPiZpY\nz6phF692vSBW4gs4syZbzJuWzTKDlos+zvSAXWN90A7ov3RdxC48saAB2vaoGatt\nrkAZC0Fttt2gpmexDJc42KXQefugoLq9fjSVc0RPwgklQ/ThlUeUikLYnv4m2T1Y\nOI+LnoyNjCIm2VhLA+0h9pa+vsVZ5o3EBPn+eduGcCtiCVNh3uHdpojn0oaQ0ebd\nxMdWYpYPVrFJSHmF+GsY\n=gJnt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T17:07:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commit/d48b9aa7017e7003b0503a15a79918ff1a3ca061","node_id":"C_kwDOU-VlpNoAKGQ0OGI5YWE3MDE3ZTcwMDNiMDUwM2ExNWE3OTkxOGZmMWEzY2EwNjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commit/021863f88f475a3aee24c694be7ec5bda8b3a867","sha":"021863f88f475a3aee24c694be7ec5bda8b3a867","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/021863f88f475a3aee24c694be7ec5bda8b3a867"}],"sha":"d48b9aa7017e7003b0503a15a79918ff1a3ca061","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/d48b9aa7017e7003b0503a15a79918ff1a3ca061"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64836476?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman","id":64836476,"login":"sam-bowman","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0ODM2NDc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/021863f88f475a3aee24c694be7ec5bda8b3a867/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T17:01:23Z","email":"64836476+sam-bowman@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sam Bowman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T17:01:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: add automated test suite, CI pipeline, coverage gate, and contributor templates (#1)\n\n* Add a full test suite and CI pipeline\n\nThere was no automated testing at all before this - every bug found this\nsession (presence desync, message cross-contamination, the federation\nprotocolId mismatch, the WS-reconnect-reverts-presence bug) was caught only\nby manual browser testing. Adds:\n\n- Unit tests (Vitest) for pure logic: ULID/identity parsing, Ed25519\n  federation request signing/verification, permission bitmasks, and user\n  serialization.\n- Integration tests (Vitest + supertest) running the real Express app\n  against a real Postgres database: auth, friends, DMs, presence, and the\n  federation protocol''s security checks (signature verification, timestamp\n  expiry, sender-domain spoofing, conversation-membership checks). Several\n  are regression tests written directly against this session''s bugs, each\n  commented with the original bug and why the test catches it.\n- Client tests for WsContext''s socket-reconnect behavior (the exact bug\n  fixed earlier this session) and the token-refresh logic in api/client.ts.\n- server/src/app.ts split out from index.ts (pure Express wiring, no\n  listen()) so supertest can exercise real routes without a live port.\n\nAlong the way, writing the presence test surfaced a real, previously-unknown\nbug: publicUser() always reported a user''s true presence status, including\nINVISIBLE - the live WebSocket broadcast already masked INVISIBLE as\nOFFLINE, but any REST fetch (e.g. the friends list on page load) leaked the\ntrue status, fully defeating invisible mode on refresh. Fixed by adding an\noptional viewerId to publicUser() that only reveals the true status to the\nuser themselves; the \"self\" endpoints (register/login/me/presence) now pass\nit, every other call site keeps the safe default.\n\nCI (.github/workflows/ci.yml) runs on every push/PR to master: lint,\ntypecheck+build (both workspaces, plus a dedicated typecheck of the server''s\ntest/ directory since vitest itself never type-checks), unit tests,\nintegration tests against a real postgres service container, npm audit,\ndependency-review on PR diffs, gitleaks secret scanning, and CodeQL static\nanalysis.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add coverage reporting and an enforced coverage floor to CI\n\nWires @vitest/coverage-v8 into all three test suites:\n\n- Unit (server + client): informational only, no threshold - they''re\n  intentionally narrow in scope (pure logic / two specific regression\n  areas), so a hard gate there would be more theater than signal.\n- Integration (server): enforced thresholds in vitest.integration.config.ts,\n  set a few points below the measured baseline (~49/35/53/55%) as a\n  regression floor rather than a stretch target. This is the suite that\n  actually exercises route handlers, so it''s the meaningful number.\n\nCI uploads each as a build artifact (lcov + browsable html) and the\nintegration job now fails if coverage drops meaningfully. This is what\nbacks the repo ruleset''s \"Require status checks to pass\" gate for coverage,\nin place of GitHub''s native \"Restrict code coverage\" option (unclear\ncurrently how that reads coverage data, and this is simpler and something I\ncan verify works today).\n\nAlso added poolOptions.forks.singleFork to the integration config - running\nwith coverage enabled occasionally crashed a forked worker outright on\nWindows (STATUS_ACCESS_VIOLATION, different file each time, no JS-level\nerror) during local testing. This reduced but didn''t fully eliminate it\nlocally; documented in the README as expected to be a Windows/V8-coverage\ninteraction that shouldn''t reproduce on the Linux CI runners, flagged so a\nbare \"worker exited unexpectedly\" failure there isn''t mistaken for a real\nregression.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add issue and PR templates\n\nBug report and feature request issue forms (structured YAML, not freeform\nMarkdown) tailored to this project specifically: the bug report asks which\nof the two run modes (single server vs. the two-server federation demo) and\nwhich area of the codebase, the feature request links back to the README''s\ndocumented roadmap gaps. Blank issues are disabled so reports stay\nstructured.\n\nThe PR template''s testing checklist mirrors what CI actually checks (lint,\ntypecheck+build, unit tests, integration tests) and adds what CI can''t -\nwhether tests were added, and whether the change was verified manually via\nscripts/start.ps1 or, for federation changes, scripts/start-federation-demo.ps1.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: add CLAUDE.md with contributor workflow and ruleset summary\n\nDocuments commands, repo-specific conventions (protocolId vs. db id,\npublicUser''s viewerId, WS event payload locations), the testing philosophy,\nand - since master is now protected - the branch/Conventional Commits\nworkflow and exactly what the \"Require PR\" ruleset and CI pipeline enforce,\nso this doesn''t silently drift out of sync with the actual GitHub settings.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: correct gitleaks coverage claim in README\n\nThe CI audit on PR #1 showed gitleaks only scans 4 commits (the PR''s own\ndiff range) on a pull_request-triggered run, not the full repository\nhistory as the README claimed - fetch-depth: 0 just makes history available\nto it, it doesn''t change gitleaks-action''s own default scan range. Verified\nthe pre-existing history is actually clean with a one-off manual full-repo\nscan (15 commits, no leaks) and corrected the docs to describe what the\npipeline actually does going forward: each PR''s new commits, covered once.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2271aebe14f2b61a9e5db6a73781fa24818667f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/trees/2271aebe14f2b61a9e5db6a73781fa24818667f5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/commits/021863f88f475a3aee24c694be7ec5bda8b3a867","verification":{"payload":"tree 2271aebe14f2b61a9e5db6a73781fa24818667f5\nparent 1e9947ed7ed299fce0ab52ba44343a89401310bb\nauthor Sam Bowman <64836476+sam-bowman@users.noreply.github.com> 1791306083 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791306083 +0100\n\ntest: add automated test suite, CI pipeline, coverage gate, and contributor templates (#1)\n\n* Add a full test suite and CI pipeline\n\nThere was no automated testing at all before this - every bug found this\nsession (presence desync, message cross-contamination, the federation\nprotocolId mismatch, the WS-reconnect-reverts-presence bug) was caught only\nby manual browser testing. Adds:\n\n- Unit tests (Vitest) for pure logic: ULID/identity parsing, Ed25519\n  federation request signing/verification, permission bitmasks, and user\n  serialization.\n- Integration tests (Vitest + supertest) running the real Express app\n  against a real Postgres database: auth, friends, DMs, presence, and the\n  federation protocol''s security checks (signature verification, timestamp\n  expiry, sender-domain spoofing, conversation-membership checks). Several\n  are regression tests written directly against this session''s bugs, each\n  commented with the original bug and why the test catches it.\n- Client tests for WsContext''s socket-reconnect behavior (the exact bug\n  fixed earlier this session) and the token-refresh logic in api/client.ts.\n- server/src/app.ts split out from index.ts (pure Express wiring, no\n  listen()) so supertest can exercise real routes without a live port.\n\nAlong the way, writing the presence test surfaced a real, previously-unknown\nbug: publicUser() always reported a user''s true presence status, including\nINVISIBLE - the live WebSocket broadcast already masked INVISIBLE as\nOFFLINE, but any REST fetch (e.g. the friends list on page load) leaked the\ntrue status, fully defeating invisible mode on refresh. Fixed by adding an\noptional viewerId to publicUser() that only reveals the true status to the\nuser themselves; the \"self\" endpoints (register/login/me/presence) now pass\nit, every other call site keeps the safe default.\n\nCI (.github/workflows/ci.yml) runs on every push/PR to master: lint,\ntypecheck+build (both workspaces, plus a dedicated typecheck of the server''s\ntest/ directory since vitest itself never type-checks), unit tests,\nintegration tests against a real postgres service container, npm audit,\ndependency-review on PR diffs, gitleaks secret scanning, and CodeQL static\nanalysis.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add coverage reporting and an enforced coverage floor to CI\n\nWires @vitest/coverage-v8 into all three test suites:\n\n- Unit (server + client): informational only, no threshold - they''re\n  intentionally narrow in scope (pure logic / two specific regression\n  areas), so a hard gate there would be more theater than signal.\n- Integration (server): enforced thresholds in vitest.integration.config.ts,\n  set a few points below the measured baseline (~49/35/53/55%) as a\n  regression floor rather than a stretch target. This is the suite that\n  actually exercises route handlers, so it''s the meaningful number.\n\nCI uploads each as a build artifact (lcov + browsable html) and the\nintegration job now fails if coverage drops meaningfully. This is what\nbacks the repo ruleset''s \"Require status checks to pass\" gate for coverage,\nin place of GitHub''s native \"Restrict code coverage\" option (unclear\ncurrently how that reads coverage data, and this is simpler and something I\ncan verify works today).\n\nAlso added poolOptions.forks.singleFork to the integration config - running\nwith coverage enabled occasionally crashed a forked worker outright on\nWindows (STATUS_ACCESS_VIOLATION, different file each time, no JS-level\nerror) during local testing. This reduced but didn''t fully eliminate it\nlocally; documented in the README as expected to be a Windows/V8-coverage\ninteraction that shouldn''t reproduce on the Linux CI runners, flagged so a\nbare \"worker exited unexpectedly\" failure there isn''t mistaken for a real\nregression.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add issue and PR templates\n\nBug report and feature request issue forms (structured YAML, not freeform\nMarkdown) tailored to this project specifically: the bug report asks which\nof the two run modes (single server vs. the two-server federation demo) and\nwhich area of the codebase, the feature request links back to the README''s\ndocumented roadmap gaps. Blank issues are disabled so reports stay\nstructured.\n\nThe PR template''s testing checklist mirrors what CI actually checks (lint,\ntypecheck+build, unit tests, integration tests) and adds what CI can''t -\nwhether tests were added, and whether the change was verified manually via\nscripts/start.ps1 or, for federation changes, scripts/start-federation-demo.ps1.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: add CLAUDE.md with contributor workflow and ruleset summary\n\nDocuments commands, repo-specific conventions (protocolId vs. db id,\npublicUser''s viewerId, WS event payload locations), the testing philosophy,\nand - since master is now protected - the branch/Conventional Commits\nworkflow and exactly what the \"Require PR\" ruleset and CI pipeline enforce,\nso this doesn''t silently drift out of sync with the actual GitHub settings.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: correct gitleaks coverage claim in README\n\nThe CI audit on PR #1 showed gitleaks only scans 4 commits (the PR''s own\ndiff range) on a pull_request-triggered run, not the full repository\nhistory as the README claimed - fetch-depth: 0 just makes history available\nto it, it doesn''t change gitleaks-action''s own default scan range. Verified\nthe pre-existing history is actually clean with a one-off manual full-repo\nscan (15 commits, no leaks) and corrected the docs to describe what the\npipeline actually does going forward: each PR''s new commits, covered once.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxSljCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKvkQACSEnQoM2QuO6HFYxuVa0mKE\n5ejtj5YeEtZ+nB5kb2qOwvYewXgAmAssjLMkW+UGSiMwTrMHbg/gfcJ+AksFdjC1\nKV999qBHe8Wsa6axrVSVtG1DWupJATjKfgibPVtqnWgbg/jjsimK8D4RYjsv61vX\nW7KGiev1R28mTaGXVfHoqu3Ghenl9Sv50OuGnj+UY3detakkJnZQLWri4g6xF5Fo\nZUC9QAcHT8IKz5wGCgxjj06zGzU30AkhbwdQDnWtyY74XHFsSHYfa5aWMhAkJQ4g\nuoPi4GZdj8bDRb6Kj8CP7Iilxqnm8JgIUw3E66kyQaGauSIRMNt6/CDPBT+DNXyd\n5E/Sanzf1sYddY5yAepaFcLdAySNWCAPgXMVcPrscc6pC9XNrtkGRbEHs93N3q3Q\n9220uj5hPP7eVODIZwbQw2N+2zmJKqZnggt/ge8+R7qyOtRFnkHH77Fb2D0MP8qd\naX3rP1ExsfWEY8PiBknGVVf+u27dF08LNMd8B8Dj9PTpYTf7XRmt3hOJ4ddoTLKw\nMCYMHPfnJxxI2lhVAi1rJBnSVp7tLHcxo0gSjlBmYupFDNevBPBqgLjimDXGH3Zq\nV9BkC59aYscvDC7M7f2akicz43amuuCryOWdNTDGKehYG+H43N0N1wbl70BpO4W6\n9P2KiPryXsa2ZjGojK11\n=9PqB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T17:01:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commit/021863f88f475a3aee24c694be7ec5bda8b3a867","node_id":"C_kwDOU-VlpNoAKDAyMTg2M2Y4OGY0NzVhM2FlZTI0YzY5NGJlN2VjNWJkYThiM2E4Njc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commit/1e9947ed7ed299fce0ab52ba44343a89401310bb","sha":"1e9947ed7ed299fce0ab52ba44343a89401310bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/1e9947ed7ed299fce0ab52ba44343a89401310bb"}],"sha":"021863f88f475a3aee24c694be7ec5bda8b3a867","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/021863f88f475a3aee24c694be7ec5bda8b3a867"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64836476?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman","id":64836476,"login":"sam-bowman","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0ODM2NDc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/1e9947ed7ed299fce0ab52ba44343a89401310bb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T11:52:06Z","email":"sam@bowmans.site","name":"Sam Bowman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T11:52:06Z","email":"sam@bowmans.site","name":"Sam Bowman"},"message":"Make stop-federation-demo.ps1 also stop the Postgres container\n\nMirrors stop.ps1''s behavior (docker compose down, data preserved in the\nvolume) instead of leaving the container running. Documented in the README\nthat this means it shouldn''t be run while the single-instance app is still\nmeant to stay up, since they share one container.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"17b14730ff7908877676795f524131a496f6d078","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/trees/17b14730ff7908877676795f524131a496f6d078"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/commits/1e9947ed7ed299fce0ab52ba44343a89401310bb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64836476?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman","id":64836476,"login":"sam-bowman","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0ODM2NDc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commit/1e9947ed7ed299fce0ab52ba44343a89401310bb","node_id":"C_kwDOU-VlpNoAKDFlOTk0N2VkN2VkMjk5ZmNlMGFiNTJiYTQ0MzQzYTg5NDAxMzEwYmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commit/ed89f2bd418a869a1061905f3756bb15e8827ee0","sha":"ed89f2bd418a869a1061905f3756bb15e8827ee0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/ed89f2bd418a869a1061905f3756bb15e8827ee0"}],"sha":"1e9947ed7ed299fce0ab52ba44343a89401310bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/1e9947ed7ed299fce0ab52ba44343a89401310bb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64836476?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman","id":64836476,"login":"sam-bowman","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0ODM2NDc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/ed89f2bd418a869a1061905f3756bb15e8827ee0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T11:49:38Z","email":"sam@bowmans.site","name":"Sam Bowman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T11:49:38Z","email":"sam@bowmans.site","name":"Sam Bowman"},"message":"Harden .gitignore against future accidental commits\n\nThe repo itself was already clean, but the patterns had gaps: no\ndist-ssr/, pnpm/yarn/lerna debug logs, .env.*.local, or Thumbs.db, and\n.vscode/ was blanket-ignored instead of allowing a shared\nextensions.json. Mirrors (and extends) the coverage already present in\nclient/.gitignore.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e0b0fb2270b11f215af7ab49a9cd3d323db87de7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/trees/e0b0fb2270b11f215af7ab49a9cd3d323db87de7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/commits/ed89f2bd418a869a1061905f3756bb15e8827ee0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64836476?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman","id":64836476,"login":"sam-bowman","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0ODM2NDc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commit/ed89f2bd418a869a1061905f3756bb15e8827ee0","node_id":"C_kwDOU-VlpNoAKGVkODlmMmJkNDE4YTg2OWExMDYxOTA1ZjM3NTZiYjE1ZTg4MjdlZTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commit/ad4ef6621617fe62bf76c9629334d1f911edf7fb","sha":"ad4ef6621617fe62bf76c9629334d1f911edf7fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/ad4ef6621617fe62bf76c9629334d1f911edf7fb"}],"sha":"ed89f2bd418a869a1061905f3756bb15e8827ee0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/ed89f2bd418a869a1061905f3756bb15e8827ee0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64836476?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman","id":64836476,"login":"sam-bowman","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0ODM2NDc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/ad4ef6621617fe62bf76c9629334d1f911edf7fb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T11:29:07Z","email":"sam@bowmans.site","name":"Sam Bowman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T11:29:07Z","email":"sam@bowmans.site","name":"Sam Bowman"},"message":"Add Phase 2 MVP: real server-to-server federation\n\nTwo independently-run homeservers can now discover each other and let their\nusers send/accept federated friend requests, exchange 1:1 DMs, and see each\nother''s presence update live, all over a signed Ed25519 HTTP protocol\n(/federation/v1/*). A remote person is represented as a cached stub User row\ncarrying their real protocolId from their home server, so every existing\ntable (FriendRequest, Friendship, ConversationMember, Message.sender) handles\nfederated data through the same foreign keys it already used locally.\n\nAlso fixes a presence bug this work surfaced: SettingsPage''s refreshUser()\ncall after a presence change created a new user object, which re-triggered\nWsContext''s socket-reconnect effect and caused the server to see the user as\noffline-then-online again, silently reverting a manually-set status (e.g.\nBUSY) back to ONLINE. The effect now keys off a stable user id instead.\n\nIncludes scripts/start-federation-demo.ps1 and stop-federation-demo.ps1 for\nrunning two full stacks locally (separate databases, env files, and PID\nfiles from the regular single-instance scripts), and a distinct Vite\ncacheDir per instance to avoid dep-optimization cache collisions.\n\nVerified end-to-end: discovery, friend requests in both directions, DMs in\nboth directions, live presence in both directions, and a restart-resilience\ncheck (killing one server mid-conversation shows the other stays healthy and\nlogs the failure, with normal delivery resuming once it''s back).\n\nKnown limitations documented in the README: no durable outbox/retry queue,\nno replay-protection nonce cache, no federated group DMs/communities, and\nremote edits/deletes/reactions don''t propagate.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2adc78803ca62eaec4faef3559d27167f489d696","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/trees/2adc78803ca62eaec4faef3559d27167f489d696"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/commits/ad4ef6621617fe62bf76c9629334d1f911edf7fb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64836476?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman","id":64836476,"login":"sam-bowman","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0ODM2NDc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commit/ad4ef6621617fe62bf76c9629334d1f911edf7fb","node_id":"C_kwDOU-VlpNoAKGFkNGVmNjYyMTYxN2ZlNjJiZjc2Yzk2MjkzMzRkMWY5MTFlZGY3ZmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commit/297f1a5181c70d71322fbf2551cbd8c0280902dd","sha":"297f1a5181c70d71322fbf2551cbd8c0280902dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/297f1a5181c70d71322fbf2551cbd8c0280902dd"}],"sha":"ad4ef6621617fe62bf76c9629334d1f911edf7fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/ad4ef6621617fe62bf76c9629334d1f911edf7fb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64836476?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman","id":64836476,"login":"sam-bowman","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0ODM2NDc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/297f1a5181c70d71322fbf2551cbd8c0280902dd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T19:41:00Z","email":"sam@bowmans.site","name":"Sam Bowman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T19:41:00Z","email":"sam@bowmans.site","name":"Sam Bowman"},"message":"Fix messages from other threads leaking into the open conversation\n\nConversationPage''s \"message:created\" WebSocket handler unconditionally\nappended every incoming message to the open conversation''s list, with\nno check that the message actually belonged to it - and the server''s\nconversation-message payload didn''t even carry a conversationId to\ncheck against (channel messages did carry channelId, but conversation\nmessages had no equivalent field at all). The result: a message sent\nin any channel, or in a completely different DM, would get appended to\nwhatever conversation happened to be open, since \"message:created\" is\na single global event every subscriber receives.\n\nAdded conversationId (mirroring the existing channelId pattern) to\nevery message:created/edited/deleted/reaction event for conversation\nmessages, and now filter on it in ConversationPage the same way\nCommunityPage already filtered its own events by channelId. Also\nadded the same explicit filtering to CommunityPage''s edited/deleted/\nreaction handlers, which were relying on an incidental \"no id match,\nno-op\" safety net rather than an actual check - fine as long as every\nid stayed globally unique across the whole app, but not something to\ndepend on.\n\nVerified by opening a DM and, while it was open, posting a message in\na channel and in a *different* DM via the API: neither leaked into the\nopen thread, while a message in the correct DM still arrived normally\nand the other two correctly surfaced only as unread indicators\nelsewhere in the sidebar/rail.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f49b64859d533034d9c6fb354ab7d301917e88f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/trees/f49b64859d533034d9c6fb354ab7d301917e88f5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/commits/297f1a5181c70d71322fbf2551cbd8c0280902dd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64836476?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman","id":64836476,"login":"sam-bowman","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0ODM2NDc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commit/297f1a5181c70d71322fbf2551cbd8c0280902dd","node_id":"C_kwDOU-VlpNoAKDI5N2YxYTUxODFjNzBkNzEzMjJmYmYyNTUxY2JkOGMwMjgwOTAyZGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commit/f261e66c472fd07992d9f59f977e8595735fa36c","sha":"f261e66c472fd07992d9f59f977e8595735fa36c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/f261e66c472fd07992d9f59f977e8595735fa36c"}],"sha":"297f1a5181c70d71322fbf2551cbd8c0280902dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/297f1a5181c70d71322fbf2551cbd8c0280902dd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64836476?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman","id":64836476,"login":"sam-bowman","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0ODM2NDc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/f261e66c472fd07992d9f59f977e8595735fa36c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T19:33:30Z","email":"sam@bowmans.site","name":"Sam Bowman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T19:33:30Z","email":"sam@bowmans.site","name":"Sam Bowman"},"message":"Fix presence getting stuck offline from an unrefreshed WS token\n\nThe WebSocket reconnect loop reused whatever access token sat in\nlocalStorage, with nothing to refresh it. apiRequest refreshes on a\n401 automatically, but that only fires when a REST call happens to go\nout - an idle tab making no REST calls (just reading live WS events)\ncould sit on an expired token indefinitely. Once that token expired,\nany connection drop (a dev server restart, a network blip) would hit\nan invalid-token close from the server, and the reconnect loop would\njust retry with the same stale token forever, never succeeding - the\nuser looks logged in and their REST calls still work (those still\nself-heal), but their presence never reports back as online and they\nstop receiving live events entirely.\n\nAdded ensureFreshAccessToken() (decodes the JWT''s exp, refreshes\nproactively if it''s expired or expiring within 10s) and call it before\nevery WebSocket connect attempt, not just the first one.\n\nVerified against the real failure mode: forged an expired access token\ninto localStorage, force-dropped the live connection by restarting the\nserver, and confirmed the client refreshed its token and reconnected\non its own - presence flipped back to ONLINE without a page reload.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9f0b2eaa982d55711b56cb7130505deeaac31d4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/trees/9f0b2eaa982d55711b56cb7130505deeaac31d4a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/commits/f261e66c472fd07992d9f59f977e8595735fa36c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64836476?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman","id":64836476,"login":"sam-bowman","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0ODM2NDc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commit/f261e66c472fd07992d9f59f977e8595735fa36c","node_id":"C_kwDOU-VlpNoAKGYyNjFlNjZjNDcyZmQwNzk5MmQ5ZjU5Zjk3N2U4NTk1NzM1ZmEzNmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commit/6e9a5e0c6cc3ef1745ee71e58964365a38dcb0c7","sha":"6e9a5e0c6cc3ef1745ee71e58964365a38dcb0c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/6e9a5e0c6cc3ef1745ee71e58964365a38dcb0c7"}],"sha":"f261e66c472fd07992d9f59f977e8595735fa36c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/f261e66c472fd07992d9f59f977e8595735fa36c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64836476?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman","id":64836476,"login":"sam-bowman","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0ODM2NDc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/6e9a5e0c6cc3ef1745ee71e58964365a38dcb0c7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T19:24:56Z","email":"sam@bowmans.site","name":"Sam Bowman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T19:24:56Z","email":"sam@bowmans.site","name":"Sam Bowman"},"message":"Add channel unread indicators and custom trigger on emoticon save\n\nChannel unread tracking: a new ChannelRead(userId, channelId,\nlastReadAt) model mirrors the existing DM read-tracking, since a\ncommunity member may read #general without having read #random.\nPOST /api/v1/channels/:id/read marks one as read; community/channel\npayloads now carry an `unread` flag per channel. The sidebar bolds\nunread channel names with a dot, and the community''s rail icon gets\nthe same dot if any of its channels are unread.\n\nCustom trigger on save: EmoticonSave gains a nullable `trigger`\noverride column (null = use the creator''s original). Saving now opens\na modal showing the emoticon and its original trigger, pre-filled and\neditable, validated server-side for collisions against the saver''s own\npersonal + other saved emoticons before accepting it. The shared\nemoticon-resolution service (used for both the compose picker and\nresolving `:trigger:` in messages) now honors this override, so a\ncustom trigger works immediately in messages, not just the picker.\n\nVerified end-to-end: a message sent with a custom-trigger emoticon\nrendered correctly, and the unread dot cleared on both the channel row\nand the rail icon after opening the channel.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"085ced65b91680ebf28aeb824706c4665d065f17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/trees/085ced65b91680ebf28aeb824706c4665d065f17"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/commits/6e9a5e0c6cc3ef1745ee71e58964365a38dcb0c7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64836476?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman","id":64836476,"login":"sam-bowman","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0ODM2NDc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commit/6e9a5e0c6cc3ef1745ee71e58964365a38dcb0c7","node_id":"C_kwDOU-VlpNoAKDZlOWE1ZTBjNmNjM2VmMTc0NWVlNzFlNTg5NjQzNjVhMzhkY2IwYzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commit/625f5ae38cea46dbeb232296b6e1e9c2e62e7b6e","sha":"625f5ae38cea46dbeb232296b6e1e9c2e62e7b6e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/625f5ae38cea46dbeb232296b6e1e9c2e62e7b6e"}],"sha":"6e9a5e0c6cc3ef1745ee71e58964365a38dcb0c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/6e9a5e0c6cc3ef1745ee71e58964365a38dcb0c7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64836476?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman","id":64836476,"login":"sam-bowman","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0ODM2NDc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/625f5ae38cea46dbeb232296b6e1e9c2e62e7b6e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T19:10:54Z","email":"sam@bowmans.site","name":"Sam Bowman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T19:10:54Z","email":"sam@bowmans.site","name":"Sam Bowman"},"message":"Redesign message list to match Discord''s layout\n\nReplace the chat-bubble layout (fixed max-width, left/right split per\nsender) with Discord''s: full-width text that wraps at the panel edge\ninstead of a narrow bubble, consecutive messages from the same sender\nwithin 5 minutes grouped under one avatar/name/timestamp header, a\nhover-revealed timestamp for grouped messages, a floating hover\ntoolbar for reactions/edit/delete instead of always-visible controls,\nand date dividers between days. Also trimmed padding on the header and\ncomposer to match the less-bulky feel of the reference.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"94860434cf11325cba0be8b6e447a237e326c610","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/trees/94860434cf11325cba0be8b6e447a237e326c610"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/commits/625f5ae38cea46dbeb232296b6e1e9c2e62e7b6e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64836476?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman","id":64836476,"login":"sam-bowman","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0ODM2NDc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commit/625f5ae38cea46dbeb232296b6e1e9c2e62e7b6e","node_id":"C_kwDOU-VlpNoAKDYyNWY1YWUzOGNlYTQ2ZGJlYjIzMjI5NmI2ZTFlOWMyZTYyZTdiNmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commit/841cd3dc44fe04cdf24145f58728b5b2f078f9bd","sha":"841cd3dc44fe04cdf24145f58728b5b2f078f9bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/841cd3dc44fe04cdf24145f58728b5b2f078f9bd"}],"sha":"625f5ae38cea46dbeb232296b6e1e9c2e62e7b6e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/625f5ae38cea46dbeb232296b6e1e9c2e62e7b6e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64836476?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman","id":64836476,"login":"sam-bowman","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0ODM2NDc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/841cd3dc44fe04cdf24145f58728b5b2f078f9bd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T19:05:11Z","email":"sam@bowmans.site","name":"Sam Bowman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T19:05:11Z","email":"sam@bowmans.site","name":"Sam Bowman"},"message":"Fix emoticons invisible to recipients; add missing UI from testing\n\nEmoticon visibility bug: messages only stored \":trigger:\" as text, and\nrendering looked it up against the *viewer''s own* emoticon library -\nso anyone who hadn''t already saved that emoticon just saw raw text\ninstead of the image. Fixed by resolving emoticons server-side against\nthe *sender''s* accessible set at read time and embedding the resolved\nimage/name/allowSave in the message payload, so any recipient sees it\nregardless of their own collection. Rendered emoticons are now\nclick-to-save for the viewer.\n\nUI gaps found in manual testing, now addressed:\n- Messages are left-aligned for everyone (was bubble-style right/left\n  split), with the sender''s name always shown.\n- Block/Unblock wired up on the Friends page, plus a Blocked tab.\n- Leave DM/group and leave community, via a proper in-app confirm\n  modal (native confirm() blocked automated testing and didn''t match\n  the rest of the UI, so it''s gone entirely).\n- Channel creation and a community settings modal (rename/description),\n  gated to the owner; new PATCH /api/v1/communities/:id endpoint.\n- Unread tracking: ConversationMember.lastReadAt, a mark-as-read call\n  on opening a chat, and an unread indicator in the sidebar.\n- Fixed a fallout bug: if the other party leaves a DM, the sidebar\n  used to fall back to showing yourself as \"the other member\" - now\n  shows \"(left)\".\n- Auth form now surfaces the actual validation error (e.g. password\n  too short) instead of a bare \"invalid_request\" code.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8053f651799aedc64e08db1ddfa3b5420705ffbd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/trees/8053f651799aedc64e08db1ddfa3b5420705ffbd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/commits/841cd3dc44fe04cdf24145f58728b5b2f078f9bd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64836476?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman","id":64836476,"login":"sam-bowman","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0ODM2NDc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commit/841cd3dc44fe04cdf24145f58728b5b2f078f9bd","node_id":"C_kwDOU-VlpNoAKDg0MWNkM2RjNDRmZTA0Y2RmMjQxNDVmNTg3MjhiNWIyZjA3OGY5YmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commit/a25471a0b4e0ffc7ab15aba87138b47d6c936359","sha":"a25471a0b4e0ffc7ab15aba87138b47d6c936359","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/a25471a0b4e0ffc7ab15aba87138b47d6c936359"}],"sha":"841cd3dc44fe04cdf24145f58728b5b2f078f9bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/841cd3dc44fe04cdf24145f58728b5b2f078f9bd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64836476?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman","id":64836476,"login":"sam-bowman","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0ODM2NDc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/a25471a0b4e0ffc7ab15aba87138b47d6c936359/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T19:04:58Z","email":"sam@bowmans.site","name":"Sam Bowman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T19:04:58Z","email":"sam@bowmans.site","name":"Sam Bowman"},"message":"Fix presence getting permanently stuck online\n\nTwo compounding bugs in the WebSocket gateway meant a user''s presence\ncould get stuck ONLINE forever:\n\n- The connection handler attached its ''close'' listener after an\n  awaited presence DB write. If the socket died during that window,\n  the ''close'' event fired with nothing listening for it yet (Node''s\n  EventEmitter doesn''t queue events for late listeners), silently\n  orphaning the connection. Fixed by registering every listener\n  synchronously before any await.\n- Presence is tracked in-memory per process with no persistence\n  reconciliation, so any dev reload, crash, or redeploy left whoever\n  was online at that instant stuck that way forever, since the new\n  process has no socket left to ever close. Fixed by resetting all\n  presence to OFFLINE on boot (reconnecting clients flip back to\n  ONLINE within seconds).\n\nAlso added a ping/pong heartbeat as a backstop for connections that\ndie silently at the network level (wifi drop, laptop sleep) without\never delivering a TCP close to the server.\n\nVerified with a raw WebSocket client killed at the TCP level mid-test:\npresence now flips to offline within milliseconds instead of never.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"163fddbbab99bcb34d089807f2cb8cd121ce2f38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/trees/163fddbbab99bcb34d089807f2cb8cd121ce2f38"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/commits/a25471a0b4e0ffc7ab15aba87138b47d6c936359","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64836476?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman","id":64836476,"login":"sam-bowman","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0ODM2NDc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commit/a25471a0b4e0ffc7ab15aba87138b47d6c936359","node_id":"C_kwDOU-VlpNoAKGEyNTQ3MWEwYjRlMGZmYzdhYjE1YWJhODcxMzhiNDdkNmM5MzYzNTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commit/27c66dd78e2dc9d8a66fdefa75003dbfc1e5e7ee","sha":"27c66dd78e2dc9d8a66fdefa75003dbfc1e5e7ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/27c66dd78e2dc9d8a66fdefa75003dbfc1e5e7ee"}],"sha":"a25471a0b4e0ffc7ab15aba87138b47d6c936359","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/a25471a0b4e0ffc7ab15aba87138b47d6c936359"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64836476?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman","id":64836476,"login":"sam-bowman","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0ODM2NDc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/27c66dd78e2dc9d8a66fdefa75003dbfc1e5e7ee/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T18:24:17Z","email":"sam@bowmans.site","name":"Sam Bowman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T18:24:17Z","email":"sam@bowmans.site","name":"Sam Bowman"},"message":"Add start/stop scripts for local dev\n\nscripts/start.ps1 brings up Docker Desktop + Postgres, creates .env\nfiles from the .env.example templates on first run, installs deps,\napplies Prisma migrations, and launches the server and client as\nbackground processes with PID files for clean teardown.\nscripts/stop.ps1 kills those processes and stops/removes the Postgres\ncontainer without touching the data volume.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"85ed5f93fc24879a310110cb11b67fa0c399744b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/trees/85ed5f93fc24879a310110cb11b67fa0c399744b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/commits/27c66dd78e2dc9d8a66fdefa75003dbfc1e5e7ee","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64836476?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman","id":64836476,"login":"sam-bowman","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0ODM2NDc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commit/27c66dd78e2dc9d8a66fdefa75003dbfc1e5e7ee","node_id":"C_kwDOU-VlpNoAKDI3YzY2ZGQ3OGUyZGM5ZDhhNjZmZGVmYTc1MDAzZGJmYzFlNWU3ZWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commit/ce571de21070e61d9d814ead162b7debccd6fc79","sha":"ce571de21070e61d9d814ead162b7debccd6fc79","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/ce571de21070e61d9d814ead162b7debccd6fc79"}],"sha":"27c66dd78e2dc9d8a66fdefa75003dbfc1e5e7ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/27c66dd78e2dc9d8a66fdefa75003dbfc1e5e7ee"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64836476?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman","id":64836476,"login":"sam-bowman","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0ODM2NDc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/commits/ce571de21070e61d9d814ead162b7debccd6fc79/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T18:18:24Z","email":"sam@bowmans.site","name":"Sam Bowman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T18:18:24Z","email":"sam@bowmans.site","name":"Sam Bowman"},"message":"Scaffold MVP: single-server federation-ready chat platform\n\nNode/TypeScript + Express + Prisma/PostgreSQL backend and a React/Vite\nweb client. Implements identity (@username:domain), friends, presence,\n1:1/group DMs, communities with roles/channels, moderation basics,\ncustom emoticons (save/fork), file attachments, and resumable sync for\noffline delivery over a WebSocket + REST API. Federation itself isn''t\nimplemented yet, but protocol IDs, identity format, and the sync outbox\nare shaped so it can be added later without a rewrite.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"68b6888857bae7b4ce0c9b857c5798f9200f5f53","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/trees/68b6888857bae7b4ce0c9b857c5798f9200f5f53"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sam-bowman/federated-chat-app/git/commits/ce571de21070e61d9d814ead162b7debccd6fc79","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64836476?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-bowman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sam-bowman","id":64836476,"login":"sam-bowman","node_